Mr. Neth Pheaktra continued to campaign and meet the CPP voters in the districts of Kratie Province on the second day of the election campaign of Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council and Khan Council.
(Kratie): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Member of Central Committee and Chairman of Kratie Provincial Party Working Group and Kratie Provincial Party Committee Working Group, continued to campaign and meet CPP voters in districts of Kratie province today. May 18, 2024, the second day of the provincial council election campaign.
In a meeting with voters and members of the Cambodian People's Party in O'Kreang Sen Chey district, the party working group chairman highlighted the importance of the provincial, municipal, district and khan council elections, as a demonstration of the maturity and robustness of the democratic process in O'Kreang Sen Chey district. Basic.
The Chairman of the Working Group called on all constituencies in Kratie to vote for the CPP so that the CPP can continue to lead the provincial councils to maintain peace and development in Kratie.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Chairman of the Kratie Provincial Party Working Group, said that the members of the Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Councils have played an important role in contributing to the maintenance of the country's peace and the development of the sub-national administration.
At the same time, the Chairman of the Working Group thanked the voters who are members of the commune council in the position of the Cambodian People's Party in O'Kreang Sen Chey district, who voted for the Cambodian People's Party in the election of the fifth mandate senator. In February 2024, the Cambodian People's Party won the election and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the party's president, was elected by the Senate to be the President of the Senate.
According to the report of Mr. Chhea Phally, Chairman of the Party Committee of O'Kreang Sen Chey District, in the commune council election in 2022, the Cambodian People's Party O'Kreang Sen Chey won 22 out of 25 seats, including 5 commune chiefs. In the last district council election, the CPP won 15 out of 15 seats, controlling and directing the O'Kreang district council.
The Swiss government has already announced that it will host a peace summit in Ukraine in mid-June, but has confirmed that Russia will not be present. It is also unclear whether China will join, with Beijing saying in the past that much needs to be done before the summit and that all parties, including Russia, be involved. Should be present to attend.
"Chinese leaders believe that if Russia loses the war ... it is a victory for the United States, a victory for him," Zelensky said in an interview with AFP on Friday. "The West and they want to find a balance between the two sides (China and the West), so I want to see China attend the peace summit."
Zelensky's remarks came as Russian President Vladimir Putin visited China, where he and President Xi Jinping claimed that relations between the two countries not only serve the fundamental interests of both countries. Not only two, but also contribute to world peace.
