Vietnamese government asks National Assembly to postpone debt owed by Vietnam Airlines
The State Bank of Vietnam, the central bank of Vietnam, provided the interest-free loan to Vietnam Airlines in 2021 to help the company recover after a two-year Kovid crisis when most flights Has been deleted. This debt is repayable within three years.
Vietnamese lawmakers also gave the airline the green light to issue shares to existing shareholders to raise 8 trillion VND (about 314 million USD). By the end of 2023, Vietnam Airlines lost 40 trillion VND.
Ministry of Water Resources announces weather conditions in Cambodia for May 18, 2024
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia for May 18, 2024.
Russia does not have enough infantry to advance its occupation of Ukraine, NATO Commander-in-Chief Christopher Cavoli said on Thursday. The assessment was reportedly based on a direct review of Russia's infantry offensive campaign on the new battlefield in Khakiv province, which began on Friday, May 10 last week.
The 278-square-kilometer attack in the new battlefield of Khakiv province is considered a Russian victory in the battle because since the launch of the offensive operation on Ukraine on February 24, 2022. Then, in just five days of military operations, Russia gained control of Ukraine for the first time.
At the same time, as the Battle of Khakiv became hot, President Zelensky canceled all foreign reception and even canceled his visit to Spain. Zelinsky was seen to be paying close attention to plotting to oust Russian forces from a village in the Kharkiv region.
Heavy fighting erupts in northern Gaza as Israel defends in international court
Hamas militants have reportedly launched an attack on Israeli tanks gathered around the southern city of Rafah. Eyewitnesses reported that Israeli armored vehicles were moving into the heart of Jabalia, Gaza's largest refugee camp, with bulldozers demolishing houses and shops on their way. .
Amid the ongoing violence, the US military confirmed the arrival of humanitarian aid trucks to Gaza, as residents expressed frustration over the destruction of residential areas despite aid efforts.
Satellite company says Ukrainian raid on Russian air base in Crimea destroys three Russian warplanes
Ukraine has turned to drones and long-range missiles to strike strategic targets behind the front lines, including the Crimean peninsula, which Russian forces captured and annexed in 2014. The recent attacks indicate an escalating conflict between the two countries, with Ukraine demonstrating its ability to reach key military targets far from the front lines.
Mr. Panh Khem Bunthorn and Banteay Meanchey Deputies Lead the 4th Mandate Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Council Election Campaign in Poipet City
The opening ceremony of the campaign was attended by the Vice President and members of the working group of the Cambodian People's Party to help Poipet City and the working group to visit the 5 Sangkats of Poipet City, as well as the leadership of members of the Cambodian People's Party in Lots of live crowds, remarkably crowded.
Keat Hul, Chairman of Poipet City CPP Committee, reported on the work plan and work progress of Poipet City Party Committee. After that, Mr. Kheng Som read the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party.
Dr. Panh Khem Bunthorn brought greetings from Samdech Techo Hun Sen to the candidates for the election and to the members of the Cambodian People's Party who actively participated in the process of building the defense of the motherland in the spirit of unity for independence, peace, freedom and democracy. Neutrality and social progress.
Minister Neth Pheakdra: Public services are an important part of serving the people of the commune and district administrations
(Kratie): "Public services are an important part of serving the people of the commune and district administrations. "We must all strive to provide public services to the people in a timely, convenient and efficient manner to strengthen people's trust."
This is the statement of Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information and Chairman of the Royal Government Working Group on Kratie Province on the afternoon of May 17, 2024, during the inspection of public administration services and visiting officials who are working. At O Kreang Sen Chey District Hall, Kratie Province.
O'Kreang Sen Chey district was established by the Royal Government of Cambodia on December 23, 2022, with five communes from Sambo district: Kbal Damrey commune, O'Kreang commune, O'Kandear Senchey commune, Rolous Meanchey commune and Sre Chik commune. Nearly 40,000 people live.
According to the Royal Government's sub-decree, the administrative location of "O Kreang Sen Chey district" must be in O'Kreang commune. The government has confirmed that the structure and administrative system of O'Kreang Sen Chey district must comply with the law on the administration of the capital, provinces, municipalities, districts and Khans. The establishment of the new district "O Kreang Sen Chey" has made Kratie province now has 1 city and 6 districts.
The Minister of Information and Chairman of the Kratie Provincial Government Working Group praised all the officials of the district hall for their dedication and hard work in serving the people.
According to O'Kreang Sen Chey district officials, about 100 people come to the public service every day.
Mr. Neth Pheakdra encouraged district officials to continue to pay attention to providing public services to the people through the OWSO and to solve the problems that the villages and communes have, especially to cooperate with stakeholders to organize public forums with People to grasp the challenges that arise.
The President of the Company also informed the President that the Company has also contributed to the training of Cambodian engineers through the training of skills in Korea to meet the actual needs of factories in Cambodia.
