(Phnom Penh): The Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture, in collaboration with the Association for the Development of Financial Institutions in the Asia-Pacific Region (ADFIAP), organized the 47th Annual Meeting under the theme “The Role of Development Financial Institutions in a Sustainable Financial Ecosystem. "The road to the future with climate resilience and sustainability."
With the participation of more than 400 delegates representing 111 Development Financial Institutions (DFIs) from 30 countries in the Asia-Pacific region, the meeting was successfully concluded with many achievements.
Outcomes of the meeting include:
* Global Cooperation: The meeting focused on promoting global cooperation among development financial institutions, policy makers and stakeholders to address urgent issues facing efforts to achieve a viable future. By sustainability. This collaboration aims to motivate stakeholders and find innovative solutions to build a climate resilient future.
* Climate resilience and adaptation: This meeting highlighted the importance of resilience and adaptation to climate change in financial strategy. Development Financial Institutions has shared its efforts to finance resilience projects such as infrastructure development projects, renewable energy initiatives and climate resilient agriculture, which will help mitigate the impacts of resilience. Climate change.
* Food Security: The meeting raised the challenges of food security caused by climate change. Development Financial Institutions agree that food security is a high priority in addressing and promoting green financing to build a climate resilient and sustainable future.
* Innovative financial instruments: The meeting discussed innovative financial instruments and mechanisms for raising capital for sustainable development projects, including: green bonds, environmentally and socially impacted investments and mechanisms. Share risk to attract private sector investment to achieve sustainable development goals.
Addressing the shortage of green financing: The ADFIAP Board encourages and calls on developed countries to increase their funding package for LDCs to address climate change and promote inclusive development. Sustainability.
* Capacity building and knowledge sharing: The meeting focused on capacity building and knowledge sharing, which helps to provide the necessary skills to development financial institutions and stakeholders to support the implementation of sustainable financing projects. Workshops, training sessions and practical sharing forums will raise awareness of the principles and strategies for implementing sustainable financing.
Dr. Kao Thach, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the Bank for Rural Development and Agriculture, said: Positive and resilient economy building across the Asia-Pacific region. "The meeting is proud of the spirit of cooperation and exchange of experience in solving innovative challenges."
During the meeting, Dr. Kao Thach also received two awards, the first for the "Intelligent Agriculture Financing Program" for the Rural Development and Agriculture Bank and the second for the "Outstanding Individual in Among the leaders of financial institutions for development "for himself. Spokesman of the General Commission: Another 323 vehicles were inspected and fined on May 17, 2024
