Malaysia's economy grows 4.2% in first quarter
KUALA LUMPUR: Malaysia's economy grew 4.2 percent in the first quarter of 2024 from a year earlier, higher than expected, government and central bank data showed on Friday. Storage of the market due to rising household costs and high exports. According to Reuters.
Economists surveyed by Reuters forecast that Malaysia's gross domestic product will grow by 3.9% between January and March this year, in line with estimates by the Malaysian Bureau of Statistics. Economic growth in the last quarter of 2023 compared to the fourth quarter of 2022 was adjusted to slow down to 2.9%.
