General knowledge: How important is philosophy to society?
(Phnom Penh): In this 5th video, Mr. Sar Rithy, PhD candidate of Philosophy of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, came in to explain another short general knowledge related to the importance of philosophy for scholars as well as in each society.
Mr. Sar Rithy said that philosophy is very important for students of philosophy for all intellectuals because philosophy teaches people to think, analyze, use intelligence to develop ideas more broadly. "When we have an idea, we are born, we are born, we are born," he said.
Mr. Sar Rithy continued that the subject of philosophy will help promote the specialization of the subject of each student or candidate to be deeper and more scientific. It also helps prevent any harm that could be caused by inaccurate assessments to researchers.
For him, a researcher, an intellectual who studies this philosophy, it is very important to help raise awareness in society, people's understanding of right and wrong, good and bad, the most important is to know oneself. He said, "Knowing yourself is wisdom," so philosophy teaches people to reflect on themselves, to think about themselves, rather than compare themselves with others.
According to Sar Rithy, there are so many people in our world that if we want to compare with others, we can not compare, so learn to compare with ourselves to understand how we are today and how to prepare for the day. Tomorrow.
This doctoral candidate encouraged all scholars, everyone, do not stop studying, which means to study forever, even Confucius scholars still consider himself a student, so we who are not you Wisdom like him must be studied more every time we can have the opportunity.
