In the second week of May, the Apsara Authority inspected and provided technical assistance to the old residents in the Angkor resort in a total of 232 cases.
(Siem Reap): In the second week of May 2024, the team inspected and monitored the construction of the residents, the old residents inspected and provided technical specifications for the construction of 232 previously approved permits and minor repairs. Case.
Out of 232 cases, 155 cases were built and repaired properly according to the permit, 76 cases were not built and repaired yet, and 1 case was built and repaired incorrectly according to the permit.
In case the people do not build according to the permit, the team facilitates them to renovate or stop the construction immediately. The technical team will continue to monitor the construction and repair until the permit expires and the construction is one hundred percent complete. .
Please be informed that the people living in Angkor Park, who are old residents, must get a building permit in accordance with the law, which is valid for one year and minor repairs (by the community working group) are valid for 3 months. All the buildings that are still valid have been inspected and provided free of charge by the Department of Land Management, Municipal and Community Heritage of APSARA Authority on a regular basis until they are one hundred percent complete.
