BEIJING: China said on Thursday that US and European claims of China's overcapacity were "clear trade protections" for their trade and that efforts to curb them New energy exports from China will affect global efforts to tackle climate change. According to Reuters.
Rising claims of China's overcapacity in industrial production, which is flooding the EU with low-cost products, are triggering a new Western-era trade war with Beijing that began with the withdrawal. Tariffs on goods imported from China by Washington in 2018.
"A country can not be defined as overcapacity just because it has more capacity than demand," Commerce Ministry spokesman He Yadong was quoted as saying by Reuters. "Production and consumption are global and supply and demand need to be matched and adjusted to the global vision," he said.
On Tuesday, Zhou Biden's government introduced measures to raise tariffs on $ 18 billion worth of Chinese-US exports, including a four-fold increase in tariffs on China's new energy vehicles.
"The countries involved are concerned about their competitiveness and market share," he added. "Overcapacity is not a product, it is a concern."
