Ministry of Culture Holds Consultation and Input Collection Workshop for 4-Year Report on the Implementation of the 2005 Convention on the Protection and Promotion of Cultural Diversity
(Phnom Penh): In the morning of May 17, 2024, at the Angkor Wat Hall of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, a consultative and input gathering workshop was held to prepare a four-year report on the implementation of the 2005 Convention on the Protection and Protection of the Kingdom. Promote cultural diversity under the chairmanship of Ms. Pen Moni Makara, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts.
The workshop was attended by representatives of UNESCO Phnom Penh, members of the 2005 Convention Team, relevant ministries / institutions, civil society organizations, technical experts, as well as officials from about 80 units under the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts.
As a party to the 2005 Convention, Cambodia is required to provide a quarterly report to UNESCO on policies and measures adopted by Cambodia and the challenges encountered in implementing the Convention.
The three main objectives of this workshop are:
1: Dissemination of the 2005 Convention on the Protection and Promotion of Cultural Diversity 2: Strengthen the capacity of all stakeholders to oversee policy, especially the establishment of dialogue between the Royal Government and civil society organizations 3: Consultation Feedback and input from ministries, institutions, relevant units, civil society organizations, associations to provide data for the preparation of a four-year report related to the implementation of the 2005 Convention.
Mr. Vincent Abel said this during a courtesy meeting and discussion with Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate on Friday morning, May 17, 2024 at the Senate.
During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen welcomed the visiting delegation to Cambodia and hoped that the visit would further strengthen the friendship and cooperation between France and Cambodia, as Cambodia and France have close ties. We have been together for a long time.
The Chairman of the delegation expressed his pleasure to visit Cambodia. He said that in fact, he had paid six official visits to Cambodia, including a total of 10 in private, but had never met Samdech Techo. Mr. Vincent Abel expressed his pleasure to have the opportunity to meet Samdech Techo during his presidency of the Senate.
Vincent Abel said that Cambodia and France have a long history of relations, with the leaders of the two countries exchanging visits and holding consultative meetings. In particular, the visit of Prince Hun Manet to Paris at the beginning of last year was very beneficial.
It has been 12 years since he was elected chairman of the Franco-Cambodian Inter-Parliamentary Friendship Group in 2012, and he has known Cambodia through 10 visits to Cambodia. And knew the area where the Khmer community lived in France, so he knew and loved the Khmer cultural traditions that made his relationship with Cambodia flourish.
The French senator expressed his pleasure at the recent visit, seeing that the French business community, investors, investors, such as: Brad Bank, tourism companies, some companies in charge of hotel health, especially the contribution. Build a station on clean water. Vincent Abel said he was jealous of Cambodia, which has access to the Mekong River, because it basically has to pump water from the ground.
He also congratulated and thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for initiating many French companies to invest in Cambodia. He observed that in Phnom Penh, there was a lot of change, but he respected the request to maintain the balance of the national heritage, such as old buildings to be taken care of with the construction of new modern buildings.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen is pleased to hear that Mr. Vincent Apple visited 10 times in Cambodia. Samdech Techo expressed his satisfaction that linked the relationship between France and Cambodia, especially the French participation in the search for peace in Cambodia by helping to meet between the Prince and the former King Norodom Sihanouk, His Majesty the King. There is the Paris Agreement.
Samdech Techo also thanked for the investment in Bak Kheng Water Station. Samdech Techo continued that last year, Cambodia was difficult due to the shortage of water, especially in Takhmao area of Kandal province, and the company Wang Si and French technicians set up a network at the bottom of the river to send water not only in Phnom Penh, but also sent Go to the suburbs for more water.
Samdech Techo spoke about the French assistance in the field of cultural heritage, France has helped a lot, especially as a co-chair with Japan in the ICC Angkor, which has helped until it was registered in the heritage of Sambor Prei Kuk in the past. This.
Samdech Techo also described the process of shifting from the old generation to the new generation, why did Samdech make sacrifices, make changes while the support through elections is still high, that what Samdech sacrificed is to maintain stability For a long time, the prince was happy that the change went smoothly.
Samdech Techo said that the results have been clear, in the past eight months, things have gone smoothly, with the economy still growing, with last year's economic growth of about 5.6 percent, and this year is expected to increase to six. At 6 percent, inflation and the exchange rate have stabilized, and exports have risen.
He also observed that Cambodia was an independent country in its independent decision-making in relation to Cambodia's openness to the Ukraine issue. Only in areas with an open-minded attitude with France.
Regarding Cambodia's rich heritage sector, Mr. Vincent Abel suggested that the influx of tourists should be encouraged, but should be organized so that tourists can stay longer as a museum. In this regard, he met with the Minister of Culture and he plans to build a museum near the Koh Ker temple for tourists to visit both the temple and the museum.
