The following is the Royal Decree: Council for the Development of Cambodia and Mondulkiri Provincial Administration held a seminar to disseminate the law on investment
(Mondulkiri): This morning, May 17, 2024, the Council for the Development of Cambodia and the Mondulkiri Provincial Administration organized a seminar on disseminating laws and regulations related to investment in Cambodia to relevant government officials in Mondulkiri. Kiri. This workshop is designed to strengthen the understanding and capacity of provincial officials involved in investing in Cambodia.
The workshop was organized and chaired by Mr. Try Dalux, Deputy Secretary General of the Cambodian Investment Committee of the Council for the Development of Cambodia and attended by Mr. Oum Khorn, Member of Mondulkiri Provincial Council, Mr. Nuon Saran, Deputy Governor. Mondulkiri Province, representatives of Mondulkiri Provincial Chamber of Commerce, traders and representatives of relevant departments under the provincial administration, a total of 86 people.
Mr. Nuon Saran expressed his deep gratitude and pleasure for the presence of the delegation of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, which organized this important seminar, and informed about the geographical, demographic, and achievements related to investment, potential and economic situation of Cambodia. Mondulkiri Province.
Speaking at the opening of the seminar, Mr. Try Dalux stated that the main purpose of the workshop was to raise awareness of the laws and regulations related to transparent investment, especially the procedures of law enforcement and relevant legal documents to the management. And officials of Mondulkiri Provincial Investment Sub-Committee.
Deputy Secretary General continued that through the above laws and sub-decrees, the Mondulkiri Provincial Investment Sub-Committee has received the authority to review and decide on the registration, incentives, guarantees, purchases, The sale, merger, delisting, and settlement of disputes involving private investment projects with an investment capital of US $ 5 million or less. This is an extension of the jurisdiction of the Capital and Provincial Investment Sub-Committee.
In addition, Mr. Try Dalux strongly hopes that through today's workshop, participants will gain the knowledge to exercise their authority with professional ethics and a high sense of responsibility.
During the workshop, the Deputy Secretary-General also brought souvenirs, including a krama, a budget of 100,000 Riels per person, and a series of documents, including investment-related laws and regulations, as well as a presentation by the speakers. .
The participants in the workshop showed great interest and enthusiastic questions, as well as expressed their deep appreciation and deep gratitude to the Council for the Development of Cambodia for initiating this important workshop.
