Dr. Eang Sophalleth is optimistic that the campaign "Clean Cambodia, Khmer can do" will spread throughout the country to make Cambodia clean
(Tbong Khmum): Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, expressed his belief and optimism that the campaign "Cambodia is clean, Khmer can do" will spread throughout the country to make Cambodia clean without pollution by plastic bags.
The Minister of Environment said: "And hope that the campaign will spread throughout the country to make our homes clean for the country to attract tourists and investors to make people better. "This campaign (Cambodia is beautiful, Khmer can do it) will be successful because before starting the campaign, three communes in Ou Raing Ov district have been tested by collecting about 4 tons of garbage."
At the same time, Dr. Eang Sophalleth expressed the expectation that the campaign "Cambodia is clean, Khmer can do" will be successful within one year. On behalf of the Ministry of Environment, he will try to make sure that people in all communes across Cambodia come out to clean the environment, pick up garbage around houses, schools, hospitals, pagodas at least once or three times a year that will make Cambodia is beautiful.
Minister Eang Sophalleth added that Cambodia has reduced its plastic imports by about 75 percent, and if so, through the launch of campaigns, it would have been possible to reduce plastic bag pollution more effectively.
"I am very optimistic because our people are starting to love the environment, he has a sprout of cleanliness in his mind, and especially in the student community, he wants to see his school clean. I understand we can finish the first step in every commune. All came out to collect and clean plastic waste before one year. This is an additional emphasis of Dr. Eang Sophalleth.
At the same time, Dr. Eang Sophalleth said that the Ministry of Environment has provided two bins to 44 schools in Ou Raing Ov district, including one bin for plastic waste and one for bins. More for general garbage storage. Separately, in health centers and pagodas also get two bins the same to make it easier to store garbage.
The Minister also stated that the goal of the Ministry of Environment is to distribute garbage to all schools across the country, but for the distribution of bins is done in stages.
