The ICAPP was established in Manila, Philippines in September 2000 to promote exchanges and cooperation among ideological political parties in Asia and Oceania. The ICAPP aims to strengthen mutual understanding and increase regional trust and promote peace and prosperity through the unique role and network of political parties.
ICAPP is committed to achieving the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals by raising awareness of key issues and fostering dialogue on the design and implementation of policies that can bring about positive change. In 2018, UNESCO recognized the ICAPP as an international organization of independent political parties and signed the "Cooperation Agreement between UNESCO and ICAPP".
ICAPP will continue to play its role not only in building a cohesive community in Asia, but also in contributing to the pursuit of world peace and prosperity.
