Thai rice rises to three-month high as Indian rice prices remain unchanged
BANGKOK: Thai rice export prices hit a three-month high due to weak supply and strong demand, while Indian rice export prices remained stable due to weak demand. According to Reuters.
A Bangkok-based trader told Reuters the increase was due to declining supply. The trader added that there was strong demand from flood-hit Indonesia and Brazil.
Flooding of farms and towns in southern Brazil has killed people, livestock, stranded infrastructure and is hampering grain shipments to local processing plants and the port of Rio Grande.
Another Bangkok-based trader said domestic demand and activity was also volatile and new supplies would arrive in July.
Did you know? The National Archives of Cambodia, a warehouse of tens of thousands of documents from Cambodia, is 98 years old as of this year
(Phnom Penh): The Department of National Archives or National Archives of Cambodia was established in 1926 and as of 2024, the repository of tens of thousands of documents from Cambodia is 98 years old. This historic building is located behind the National Library of Cambodia.
It is an institution of the Royal Government under the control of the Office of the Council of Ministers. The National Archives Department is responsible for managing and maintaining the Royal Government's administrative documents of historical and legal value for preservation for current and future use.
Documents contained in the Department of National Archives record events and decisions that reflect the state and society of Cambodia since the 19th century. The National Archives of Cambodia manages documents created or collected by the French colonial administration and the administrative documents of the Royal Government from its national independence to the sub-national level, covering a wide range of topics over the past two centuries. Come on.
The National Archives of Cambodia has made great efforts to preserve and restore the documents of national history and to disseminate the knowledge and techniques of document preservation to the officials of state institutions to jointly preserve the national history.
The National Archives of Cambodia is a public institution that welcomes all members of the public who wish to study, explore and research Cambodia's past. The National Archives of Cambodia welcomes Panhavorn students, researchers, educators, government officials and the general public to study our rich literature.
