The following is the sub-decree of the Prime Minister:
Political diplomacy is an important task in the policy of the new government led by Samdech Maniphea Hun Manet. Visiting South Korea is no different from visiting other countries, not to mention the business forum, which is an important forum for attracting investment.
The Cambodia-Republic of Korea Business Forum, organized by the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Chamber of Commerce and Industry of the Republic of Korea, was attended by more than 300 Cambodian and Korean investors representing 198 companies.
Despite being busy with the meeting program, President Hun Manet presided over the opening of the forum and presented policies related to investment in Cambodia to attract Korean investors to Cambodia.
The Prime Minister also highlighted the Royal Government's policy of providing high support for the private sector and foreign investment, as well as Cambodia's economic situation, which improved before the outbreak of Kovid 19, which maintained growth. Around 7% for about two decades and is recovering well after the 19 Kovid outbreak.
According to Hun Manet, the first new initiative is to establish a consultation mechanism where Korean businesses can meet with the Council for the Development of Cambodia twice a year. The meeting aims to provide an opportunity for Korean businesses to meet directly with government agencies responsible for investment twice a year.
He confirmed that Cambodia had held such meetings with Japan and established this business community in the United States and Europe. He stressed that Cambodia is now establishing a Korean business and investment community in Cambodia to ensure that investors' problems are addressed and investors work together to find timely solutions because Cambodia cares about existing businesses. Already in Cambodia.
"Our model is to protect what is already there while attracting something new. If we can not protect existing businesses in Cambodia and create an environment for them to grow, then we do not expect to attract new investment. This is true. "So this is a government priority." This is the confirmation of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet related to the first initiative.
The second initiative is to create an exclusive special economic zone for Korean companies. President Hun Manet stated that this aims to create an environment where Korean businesses can create ecosystems or supply chain models that the Cambodian government can partner with to provide timely solutions to the Korean business community. He said a working group between Korea and Cambodia could be set up soon.
President Hun Manet expressed hope that through this new initiative, more businesses and the private sector from Korea will seek Cambodia as a good partner for investment and business.
The Republic of Korea is one of Cambodia's largest trade and investment partners with a total bilateral trade volume of approximately $ 751 million, ranking 11th in 2023. In addition, direct investment from the Republic of Korea (FDI) totaled more than $ 5 billion, totaling about $ 30 million, ranking ninth in 2023.
