Health Officer: 5 points that all nurses must follow to contribute to the promotion of quality patient care services
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Un San, Deputy Director of the Department of Health Protection and Chairman of the Board of Nurses of Cambodia, said that nurses are the ones who are in direct contact with the patients who are most aware of their well-being and development. Must have sufficient capacity to contribute to the provision of quality care and health care services to patients and citizens.
His remarks at the opening of the training course on "Cambodian Nurses' Ethics and Standards of Practice of Nurses" held at Preah Ang Duong Hospital under the chairmanship of Professor Lou Ly Kheang, Director of Preah Ang Duong Hospital On May 16, 2024.
Mr. Un San said that nurses are the driving force of the Ministry of Health, which is the driving force to effectively and efficiently provide quality care services and improve the health of patients and people. Therefore, the ability of nurses to adhere to is 5 points:
1: Properly apply professional ethics, if not properly applied means that the nurse is incompetent and will affect the patient 2: Must have leadership and management in care 3: Must be educated Research and practice 4: Must strengthen their profession and continue training to develop skills 5: Must strengthen the profession of nurse, especially to apply in the hospital
"The five capabilities that we have strengthened and implemented properly, we will have the quality to provide care management services to patients really." On that occasion, he also urged all nurses to be registered and properly licensed.
Meanwhile, Professor Lou Ly Kheang said he was happy that staff at Ang Duong Hospital had received their second training this year. The director of the hospital also urged his staff to be well-mannered and attentive in this important training to be successful.
"Nursing staff, as well as other departments in the past, always adhere to professional ethics and speak kindly to patients, but at the same time we must continue to learn more," he added. To develop themselves continuously and fill any gaps.
At the same time, Prof. Luli Kheang expressed his deep gratitude to Master Un San for taking the time to train all the nurses of Ang Duong Hospital. That this training will continue to be so that nurses, nurses and midwives have a better ethics and better health services for the people.
On that occasion, Ms. In Vichara, Chairman of the Nursing Committee of Ang Duong Hospital, on behalf of all nurses, was determined to perform their duties properly in a professional manner to take good care of patients with high quality.
