Ministry of Water Resources announces weather conditions in Cambodia for May 17, 2024
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia for May 17, 2024.
Low pressure covers the Gulf of Thailand, the Kingdom of Cambodia, the central Mekong Basin and the South China Sea, the ministry said. This situation will make: From 17 to 19 May 2024:
1. Lowland area: * Minimum temperature 24 ° C and maximum temperature 35 ° C. Winds from the southeast and southwest average 2.5 meters per second. Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap, Battambang, Pursat, Kampong Cham, Tbong Khmum, Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Thom, Svay Rieng, Prey Veng, Takeo, Kandal and Phnom Penh are likely to experience rain with thunder, lightning and gust covering 25% of the area.
2. Upland areas: * Minimum temperature 24 ° C and maximum temperature 35 ° C. Winds from the west and southwest have an average speed of 3.5 m / s. Oddar Meanchey, Preah Vihear, Stung Treng, Pailin, Kampong Speu, Ratanakkiri, Mondulkiri, Cardamom and Dangrek mountain ranges may experience rain with thunder and gust covering 25% of the area.
