In other words, this canal is an important part of the socio-economic development of the country through better water transport and navigation, as well as connecting the Cambodian economy to the region and the world, as well as can help release water. Flooding in the southwestern provinces is a source of water supply for Cambodians engaged in agriculture, aquaculture and facilitates the transportation of agricultural products from the provinces more easily, reducing time costs and so on.
The Prek Chik project is a project to connect waterways between rivers to the sea of Cambodia, passing through Kandal, Takeo, Kampot and Kep provinces with a total length of about 180 km. The project is expected to cost about $ 1.7 billion and will be studied in detail over a period of 26 months.
This project was approved by the Royal Government of Cambodia for the sixth term in 2023, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, and also supported by the new Royal Government led by Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet. Both Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet have declared their strong commitment to dig the Funan-Techo canal for economic benefits, especially the connection of Cambodia's waterway between rivers and seas.
