* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Vietnamese Prime Minister had instructed Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun that Vietnam respects Cambodia's sovereignty, but also complained to some Vietnamese people on environmental issues.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Funan Techo Canal Project is a canal initiated entirely by Cambodia and China is unaware of this.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Funan Techo canal project is not part of China's belt and road project.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Funan Techo canal is in the economic interest and political independence of Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen insisted on stopping anti-Chinese politics by linking the canal issue with Vietnam's security.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia has good relations with Vietnam, Vietnam has good relations with China, so there is no reason to go to war against each other.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the 1995 agreement on the Mekong River, Cambodia must notify the Joint Commission and there is no need to consult or negotiate with the Mekong River Commission.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it was polite for both Samdech and Samdech Techo to inform the Vietnamese side. But according to the law, Cambodia is not required to consult with Vietnam.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia had planned to dig a drain from the Mekong River into the Vaiko River, but the Mekong River Commission demanded consultation, so Cambodia suspended it. Cambodia then used the small river, a tributary of the Mekong River, to dig and connect to the Vaiko River instead.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that we must consider the economic interests and independence of our nation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Funan Techo canal is very profitable for the national economy. The profit distance is 169 kilometers.
