(Kampong Chhnang): On the morning of May 16, 2024, the Cambodian-Chinese Armed Forces jointly launched the 6th Golden Dragon Exercise 2024 under the chairmanship of General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Admiral Kao Siv Ching. Deputy Chief of Staff of the Southern Region of the Chinese People's Liberation Army.
The Golden Dragon Exercise will run for 15 days from 16 to 30 May 2024 under the theme "Joint Counter-Terrorism Operation and Humanitarian Relief" with a ground exercise held at the Gendarmerie Training Center (Phnom Penh). Chum Sen Reak Reay) is located in Peam commune, Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province, and the sea exercise is located in Sihanoukville province.
Speaking on the occasion, General Vong Pisen said that the annual Golden Dragon Exercise between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army in 2024 has been expanded over previous years, the content is deeper and the number of participating troops is more and more modern. In line with the scale of cooperation between the two armies, which is growing and deepening in all fields.
According to the General, this year's Golden Dragon Exercise is not only an Army-level and ground-level exercise on land, but also an expansion to the sea, and this Golden Dragon Exercise will continue to grow and expand to the Air Force and Other types of skilled troops in the future.
The General stressed that the purpose of the Golden Dragon Exercise 2024 is to deepen the strategic partnership, comprehensive strategic cooperation, strengthen mutual political trust, serve the building of a common destiny of Cambodia and China in the new era and promote cooperation. Operation Exchange of experience between the two armies.
"The Golden Dragon exercise has become a symbol of the strong and inseparable cooperation between the two countries and the two armies, Cambodia and China. "This exercise is important to enhance the capabilities and understanding of the two armies, such as demonstrating capabilities, exchanging experiences with each other, raising awareness of joint command and operational procedures, new tactics, techniques and new skills." This is the confirmation of General Vong Pisen.
The Commander-in-Chief thanked the Chinese People's Liberation Army for assisting the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces in training human resources, building infrastructure, especially at the Army Institute, improving air defense systems, automatic missile systems and weapons. Heavy and build a modern international mixed shooting range at Phnom Chum Sen enjoy.
He said that the cooperation between the two countries has made steady progress, significantly enhancing the traditional friendly relations, in which the cooperation between the two countries' armies has been further strengthened and deepened. All sectors up to "cooperation, strategic partnership in all aspects" by trusting, understanding, respecting, helping each other and providing mutual benefits.
Regarding the exercise with foreigners, General Vong Pisen stated that the new Article 53 of the Cambodian Constitution clearly states that the Kingdom of Cambodia adheres to the policy of permanent neutrality, non-alignment and peaceful coexistence with neighboring countries and countries. All over the universe. Cambodia does not invade and does not interfere in the internal affairs of other countries, resolve all issues peacefully and respect each other's interests.
