Cambodian, Chinese troops hold 6th joint Golden Dragon exercise under joint theme "Joint counter-terrorism operation and humanitarian work"
(Phnom Penh): More than 2,000 troops of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army, accompanied by 14 warships and other military equipment, participated in the "Golden Dragon" exercise this morning, May 16, 2024. Sixth, 2024 under the theme "Joint Counter-Terrorism Operations and Humanitarian Work". The 6th Golden Dragon Exercise will be held for 14 days from 16 to 30 May 2024.
For the opening ceremony of the Golden Dragon exercise, the Cambodian side was presided over by General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, while the Chinese side was Major General Kao Sivqing, Deputy Chief of Staff of the Southern Region of the Chinese People's Liberation Army.
This is the sixth large-scale exercise between Cambodian and Chinese troops on Cambodian soil since the first exercise was held in 2016, as the two countries are strategic partners and are building a common destiny. .
According to Major General Thong Solimo, spokesman for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) Command, the 6th Golden Dragon Exercise was attended by the Cambodian Army and Navy, for the Army to be held at the Army Training Center. The Royal Gendarmerie is located in Chrak Kov village, Peam commune, Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province, and the offshore exercise is being held in Sihanoukville.
At the same time, Major General Thong Solimo said that the content of the exercise is focused on counter-terrorism and humanitarian work, in addition to focusing on drone countermeasures. The exercise also invited ASEAN countries to observe the nature of the exercise between the two armies.
The lieutenant general said that the sixth Golden Dragon exercise between the two armies was larger than the previous ones due to the large number of troops participating, as well as expanding the level of surface drills. Use up to 14 warships.
A spokesman for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) has reaffirmed that the 6th Golden Dragon Exercise 2024 between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army (PLA) in Cambodia is not intended to threaten or harm any country. . Cambodia always welcomes friendly countries that wish to conduct exercises but must respect Cambodia's rights.
The Golden Dragon exercise between Cambodia and China has been held since 2016 and so far has been six times. Both sides have suspended three times, in 2017, busy with drug crackdowns and commune council elections, and in 2021-2022, which faces the spread of Kovid 19.
