Xi Jinping, Vladimir Putin praise China-Russia relations at Beijing talks
BEIJING (Reuters) - Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin held a bilateral meeting in Beijing on Thursday on the sidelines of Putin's two-day visit to China. This was released by the AFP news agency on Thursday, May 16, 2024.
During the meeting, Xi told Putin that "China-Russia relations not only serve the fundamental interests of the two countries, but also contribute to world peace." "China is ready to work with Russia to maintain transparency and justice in the world." Xi added that Beijing is ready to build closer ties with Russia.
Putin told Xi that Russia-China relations were a force for stability in the current tumultuous world, and that the two countries' ties were not opportunistic. Or target against any other country. "Our cooperation on various international issues is a stabilizing factor on the international stage," Putin said.
(Phnom Penh): According to the Elderly Health Commission of the Ministry of Health, the percentage of the elderly in Cambodia will increase by 8.9% in 2019 and may increase to 11% by 2030 as the number of elderly people. Caused by a combination of two factors: an increase in the life expectancy of the Cambodian people and a decrease in the birth rate.
Mr. KER Ratha stated that the Ministry of Health has established the Ministry of Health's Committee on the Elderly Health through Resolution No. 008 SCN / SOR dated March 27, 2024 as a mechanism for orientation. Manage the health of the elderly effectively. This is the first meeting of the members of the Committee on Health of the Elderly of the Ministry of Health in the 7th term of the Royal Government.
He added that Cambodia has identified the elderly as people over the age of 60 (National Policy on the Elderly 2017-2030). This setting may vary depending on the situation, increasing the life expectancy of the people in the future can be set from 65 years. He said that the number of elderly people in Cambodia is evolving in line with the development of the world.
As the number of elderly people increases, so does the demand for health services, adding to the burden on the health sector, which we must prepare from now on to respond appropriately and in a timely manner.
Elderly people's health It is the result of influencing people's behavior at a young age, so education promotes health care, especially diet, exercise of young people to prepare for a healthy old age. It is an important task that this is also the task of our health sector to take care of.
The Ministry has developed an action plan for the development and promotion of the health of the elderly and has included it in a five-year action plan prepared by the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation. However, the challenge is the lack of funds to implement these action plans, so mobilizing funds from development partners to support the implementation of those activities is necessary, and choosing the priority activities to be implemented first is very important.
