On that occasion, Mr. Muth Chenda said that after the announcement of the vocational and technical training program for 1.5 million poor and vulnerable families on November 14, 2023 under the high presidency of Samdech President. Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Techo Sen Svay Rieng Polytechnic Institute, announced the recruitment and selection of municipalities, districts and communes throughout Svay Rieng province.
He added that today, 122 students, 11 girls, met all the requirements of the institute to be able to take the graduation test to prove their ability to get a technical and vocational degree in the vocational and technical training program. Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training.
He added that along with the proficiency test, about 70 percent of the students were working in factories, enterprises, garages according to their respective abilities, and about 30 percent of the institute will prepare them to complete. Work in factories, enterprises and garages, that is, all students after graduation must have a job in accordance with the noble words of Samdech Hun Sen Manet "Learn to finish to know how to get a job."
Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie Commander Distributes Water to People Living Away in Chbar Morn City
(Kampong Speu): Due to the hot weather and no rain, some villagers in Chbar Morn City, Kampong Speu Province live far from water sources and face water shortage on the morning of May 15, 2024, Brigadier General Meng Srun The Commander of the Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie led the force to distribute water to the people.
Brigadier General said that after receiving information about the shortage of daily necessities, he gave the fire truck of the unit to act as a water truck to help people in the dry season, there is not enough water for use.
"So far, the unit's trucks have been able to deliver to Tamol village, where 16 families are short of water, 10 trucks and Kandol Dom village, 15 families are short of water," he said. Use 6 water trucks. Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates agree to accelerate the implementation of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on May 15, 2024, said that Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates have agreed to accelerate the implementation of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (CEPA).
According to the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, the two sides agreed on the importance of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates to deepen bilateral cooperation.
The two sides also discussed ways to accelerate the implementation of the CEPA, which was signed in June 2023, and stressed that it would open up more markets for goods and services, increase investment flows and create jobs. Cooperation in various fields and mutual benefit.
The Deputy Prime Minister and the Ambassador expressed their appreciation for the long-standing friendship and strong cooperation between Cambodia and the United Arab Emirates since the establishment of diplomatic relations in 1994, and reaffirmed their commitment to further strengthen Further bilateral relations and provide mutual support in the international arena for the mutual benefit of both countries.
The Deputy Prime Minister and the Ambassador also exchanged views on enhancing cooperation between the two countries in the fields of trade, investment and tourism.
Samdech Hun Sen and Lok Chumteav Bandit Arrive Safely in South Korea
(South Korea): After traveling for more than 5 hours on the afternoon of May 15, 2024, His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia and HE Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet arrived in South Korea to visit. Official for 4 days from 15 to 18 May 2024.
Arriving in South Korea, the President and Lok Chumteav Dr. were warmly welcomed by senior officials of the South Korean Government, the Cambodian Ambassador to South Korea.
Accompanying the President and Lok Chumteav Bandit were Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, as well as key government officials and parliamentarians. Cambodia Business.
He will also attend the Cambodia-Republic of Korea Business Forum and meet with a number of major Korean companies. During his visit, Samdech Thipdey will also meet with the Cambodian community living, studying and working in South Korea.
After the formal establishment, relations and cooperation between the two countries have been further strengthened, expanded and enhanced.
South Korea has become one of the countries that has made significant contributions to Cambodia's development through funding for road construction, education, human resource training, health and rural development.
Through better relations, Cambodia and South Korea have also expanded trade and investment together in significant growth.
Trade between the two countries in 2023 will have a total budget of about 751 million US dollars. In the first three months of 2024, it will reach nearly 200 million US dollars.
On December 1, 2022, Cambodia and South Korea signed a free trade agreement. Through this free trade agreement, trade between the two countries will be expanded.
In terms of investment, from 1994 to the beginning of 2024, the investment from South Korea was more than 5 billion US dollars.
The current visit of Hun Manet to South Korea is expected to contribute to further enhancing cooperation, trade and investment between the two countries.
