General knowledge: What are the features of Khmer philosophy?
(Phnom Penh): Between the two ancient civilizations, India and China, Cambodia has received good philosophical influences from these two countries, but Khmer philosophy also has its own characteristics. What are the features of Khmer philosophy?
To answer these questions, Mr. Sar Rithy, a candidate for PhD in Philosophy of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and a speaker in the General Knowledge Program, also came to explain to the viewers / readers in this third video.
Mr. Sar Rithy said that if you look at the historical aspect, Cambodia is located between the two major countries, the oldest civilized superpowers, India and China. China has a culture that is more than 5,000 years old, India has a culture that is more than 4,000 years old, while Cambodia has a culture that is about 2,000 years old. More.
The Cambodian people have been in contact with people from India and China since before the time of the Mountain Kingdom or Funan, but only as a relationship between the people and the common people, not yet a diplomatic relationship, but in Give each other philosophy, while Cambodians also have their own philosophy from ancient times.
The first century saw the rise of Hinduism, and the third century saw the rise of Buddhism. The arrival of religions from India also brought with it philosophies, and the Khmer ancestors accepted both religions equally, but the greatness of the Khmer was not to accept what was not good, and what was good, the Khmer accepted and Synthesis with existing things, the point that does not fit with the attitude or idea is that Khmer do not accept.
The greatness of Khmer philosophers is the synthesis of all those religious beliefs and philosophies that coexist without conflict.
Mr. Sar Rithy compared the characteristics of the Khmer people to the sea water, that is, the sea water accepts water from rivers, streams, canals, canals, etc., but the sea does not accept coins, garbage, corpses or anything bad, that is, always This is the philosophy of the ancient Khmer people. Dr. Nuon Danhel led a delegation to inspect, evaluate and complete the construction of three road projects in Kampong Chhnang, Pursat and Kampong Speu.
