Cracking down on robberies and breaking into illegal pawnshops in Toul Kork district, confiscating some undocumented motorbikes, Criminal Police Department calls on victims who have lost their motorbikes to verify
(Phnom Penh): The Criminal Police Department cracked down on a robbery case and broke into an illegal pawn shop in Phnom Penh's Tuol Kork district, confiscating undocumented motorbikes, credit cards and other license plates.
The operation was carried out on the orders of Lt. Gen. Neng Chuor, director of the Criminal Police Department, and the light criminal bureau force, led by Brigadier General Vuthy Vongvibol, deputy director of the department, and Lt. Col. Leng Bun Hour, director of the bureau.
After receiving information about aggravated theft (motorcycle hijacking) on May 4, 2024 at Kandal Village, Sangkat Rolous, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh, under the direction of His Excellency the Director of the Criminal Police Department, assigned the specialized force of the Criminal Office Light level, lead research and investigation, as a result reach the target of activities and locations to sell motorcycles.
On May 6, 2024, the specialized force of the Criminal Police Office of the Criminal Police Department arrested six suspects from behind the palace, Sangkat Chey Chumneas, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh, and brought them to the Department for interrogation and case building.
The nine suspects also confessed that their accomplices hijacked three motorcycles and stole mobile phones from the victims in Dangkor district, Phnom Penh and Takhmao city, Kandal province. After robbing the motorcycle, Sok Samnang sold it to an unidentified person at the ammunition depot in Toul Kork district, Phnom Penh.
On May 7, 2024, the suspect named Sok Samnang pointed out the suspect who bought the motorcycle from him at the ammunition depot in Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh, and the police arrested Song Serey, male, 43 years old. Address: House for rent, Room 9, Street Lum, Sangkat Boeung Tumpun, Khan Meanchey, Phnom Penh.
Under the coordination of Mr. Kim Hong San, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, the specialized force searched the place to buy and display motorcycles, warehouse 7, house 5, street 192, Sangkat Teuk Laak III, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh. There are no clear identification documents, license plates and some other credit cards to be stored at the department to build a case file.
