(Phnom Penh): On Wednesday morning, May 15, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, and his wife, Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet, led a high-level delegation to pay a four-day official visit to the country. South Korea.
The current visit of Samdech Manet to South Korea is expected to contribute to further enhancing cooperation, trade and investment between Cambodia and South Korea.
+ Diplomatic relations:
Cambodia and South Korea formally established diplomatic relations on October 30, 1997. This diplomatic bond was re-established under the strong efforts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, or Samdech Techo as a midwife, to establish relations between Cambodia and South Korea.
+ Economic cooperation:
Cambodia's main exports to Korea in 2023 include machinery and electrical equipment, footwear, clothing and accessories, aluminum, machinery and mechanical equipment, leather goods, toys, sports equipment, pharmaceutical products, plastics, paper and cardboard, rubber, fruits and nuts. Edible fruits and so on.
Cambodia's main imports from Korea in 2023 include vehicles, machinery, electrical appliances, beverages, wine and vinegar, raw leather (besides leather), leather, plastics, pharmaceuticals, other textiles, rubber, machinery and mechanical equipment.
Financing: From 1992 to 2022, South Korea provided about $ 455 million in grant funding for development in Cambodia.
From 2001 to December 2023, the South Korean government provided a total of more than $ 1.8 billion in concessional loans for 36 concessional loan agreements.
