(Phnom Penh): On the morning of May 13, 2024, the Foundation provided more than 50,000 US dollars worth of generators and 20 wheelchairs to Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hospital.
The handover ceremony was presided over by Mr. Yin Saven, Deputy Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province, Dr. Prak Von, Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department, and Karuna Silvisut, Senior Buddhist Disciple, Chay Kong, Duke Ing Bunhou and Mrs. Heng Sokha, and their families. Sambath, director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hospital, health officials, doctors, doctors and a total of about 150 people.
During the ceremony, Duke Ing Bunhou, President of the Eng Foundation, stated that seeing the shortage and necessity of using electricity when there is a power outage from the province, especially during surgery patients. In the past, doctors have used mobile phones to operate on patients when a power outage or a broken generator occurs.
The Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department, Dr. Prak Von, expressed his appreciation for the acquisition of new equipment to support the operation of medical services and rescue patients needed in the event of a power outage.
In return for the generosity of the family of Duke Ing Bunhov, the Deputy Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province calls on all doctors to help treat and save the lives of people with virtue and ethics.
In this morning's ceremony, Duke Ing Bunhov donated an additional 8 million Riels to the hospital and donated a total of 40,000 Riels to about 200 patients.
Please be informed that Karuna Silvisut, Akka Moha Upasika, Buddhist supporter Chai Kong and Duke Ing Bunhou and his family have been very supportive of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hospital. The hospital was first built in 1998 and many more, and more recently, the hospital has received a washing machine that has saved the lives of many patients.
Subsequent donations totaling approximately US $ 350,000 from 1998 to 2024, with the construction of emergency facilities and medical equipment, construction of maternity wards, red gravel water supply in the provincial hospital, especially washing machines. Two blood machines, one ultrasound machine, one water purifier and a dialysis building will be renovated in March 2023.
