General knowledge: When did philosophy start and where did it originate?
(Phnom Penh): Through the study of philosophy, we get to know many scholars, doctors, philosophers around the world, but do you know when philosophy started and where it originated?
To answer these questions, Mr. Sar Rithy, a candidate for PhD in Philosophy of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, came to explain to the audience / readers in this second video. It should be informed that in the video part 1, Mr. Sar Rithy has already shown the content of the definition of philosophy, he concluded that "philosophy is a subject for people who like to think, analyze, consider to find the truth."
Regarding the beginnings of philosophy, Sarith said that philosophy had its origins around 600 BC, known through the presence of Socrates, the ancient Greek philosopher, meaning that philosophy first appeared in Ancient Greece from about 600 BC.
In the East, philosophy first appeared in ancient China through the presence of Lao Tzu and Confucius around 500 BC. Around 500 BC, in ancient India, there was the presence of Samma Samputa, a world-famous philosopher.
Mr. Sar Rithy continued that according to the study of philosophy, it is divided into 2 poles: 1- Western pole with European countries, etc. 2- East pole, which is in China, India and later in Cambodia. Vietnam and so on.
The study of this philosophy also has many other branches, including: logic, linguistics / etymology, anthropology, aesthetics, ethics, Buddhism.
Mr. Sar Rithy added that in daily life, there is a philosophy embedded or presented, even a bottle of pure water also shows and embed philosophy in it, so every branch of this philosophy is relevant to life. Necessary.
