(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Moha Bovathi Hun Manet, has decided to assign Mr. Kitech, Chief of the Royal Government's Law Team, to protect the people and to represent the people in cases being handled by the prosecution and institutions. Court of project of former tycoon Leng Channa.
On the morning of May 15, 2024, before leaving for a four-day official visit to South Korea, President Hun Manet posted a message accompanied by a letter of authorization assigned to Mr. Kitech, which is as follows: :
To the victims of the project of former tycoon Leng Channa,
In response to the request of the affected people in the case of the project of former tycoon Leng Channa, who requested my intervention, I decided to entrust His Excellency Ky Tech, Chairman of the Royal Government's Law Team, to protect the people and to represent them. Citizens in cases being handled by the prosecution and the judiciary.
I would like to take this opportunity to clarify the subsequent actions of the Royal Government and myself in relation to this case.
As assigned, HE Say Sam Al tried to coordinate with the company in order to find a solution for the people as far as possible and as far as possible, but a solution in this way was not possible.
Authorities also investigated the case and found that Brillian City's investment project was not like any other real estate investment project, which was a real investment project and faced obstacles with downside issues. The market, but on the contrary, Leng Channa's project is a system of cheating according to the Ponzi Scheme.
Based on the results of this investigation, on March 12, 2024, I ordered the law enforcement forces to strictly enforce the law and proceed to arrest Leng Channa to be sent to court in accordance with the procedures in force.
At the same time, on March 13, 2024, I made a request to the King in the highest esteem to end the title of Duke of Ms. Leng Channa, with a Royal Decree signed by Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, Acting Head of State. On March 14, 2024.
Although the case is in the hands of the court, the Royal Government continues to monitor this case on a regular basis and has assigned the relevant authorities to continue to research and cooperate to support all court proceedings that the law allows to work together to solve problems for the people. Citizens do their best to follow the law.
We will continue to work together to find appropriate solutions for the people in accordance with the legal procedures in force.
