Analysis: Foreign capital is increasing investment in China, which shows the new attractiveness of the Chinese market
After more than 40 years of reform and opening-up, China has become the world's second largest economy and the world's largest manufacturing industry for 14 consecutive years. It has also maintained its position as the world's largest commodity trading country for seven consecutive years. Undoubtedly, in the industrial chain and global supply chain, China is an indispensable part.
Recently, Kearney, a world-renowned management and consulting firm, released its 2024 Global Foreign Direct Investment Direct Investment Index report, showing that China's rating has risen from Ranked seventh last year to third this year, China ranks first among emerging markets.
China has been adhering to a win-win and open win-win strategy, actively promoting economic globalization, welcoming enterprises from other countries to invest and do business in China. Let yourself develop and benefit the world through openness and cooperation.
In the first four months of this year, China's exports and imports amounted to 13.81 trillion yuan, up 5.7 percent year on year, according to statistics released by the General Administration of Customs. Compared to the same period of 2023. In the first four months of this year, the volume of exports and imports broke new records in the same period of history, and the positive trend of China's foreign trade was further strengthened.
As the world's second largest economy, China, which is developing sustainably and more openly, will surely bring new momentum and new opportunities for the world through its new development.
