In this meeting, Samdech Techo, President of the Senate, congratulated her on her appointment as Ambassador of Canada to the Kingdom of Cambodia. Samdech Techo hopes that in her tenure, she will make every effort to further enhance the Cambodia-Canada bilateral relations.
In terms of ASEAN work, Canada is working to find a Free Trade Agreement with ASEAN, which will benefit both ASEAN and Cambodia. Samdech Techo hopes that she will further promote the bilateral relations between Cambodia and ASEAN.
In response, the Ambassador of Canada thanked Samdech Techo for congratulating her on her appointment as Ambassador of Canada to Cambodia. She also congratulated Samdech Techo on his appointment as President of the Senate.
She will work to improve cooperation in all areas, especially with the Asian Development Bank (ADB) in the development of the solar energy sector.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that Cambodia and Canada have had a long relationship, that is, more than 70 years ago, we had diplomatic relations in 1952 before Cambodia gained independence.
Samdech said that in the past, Cambodia has always highly valued those friends who recognized Cambodia before Cambodia gained independence, which is a factor in promoting the process of Cambodia's independence. Samdech Techo continued that at that time, Canada, Poland and India were members of the Commission for the Supervision of Independence for Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pleasure to see that the trade volume of the two countries has developed steadily, despite our past challenges such as Kovid 19, geopolitical issues, trade volume has not changed significantly.
