Mr. Vongsey Visoth opened a training course on the basic principles of Khmer Constitution and Administrative Law
This training course was held on May 13, 2024 at the Office of the Council of Ministers, organized by the Legal Council of the Office of the Council of Ministers.
The training on the basic principles of Khmer Constitutional Law and Administrative Law is very important for lawyers, legal scholars and policy makers, and also responds to the roles and responsibilities of the Office of the Council of Ministers, which is responsible for coordinating the work of the Royal Government. Daily work of the entire Council of Ministers, especially on the review and revision of policies, laws and national strategic plans and legal reforms.
Mr. Ly Chantola, Vice Chairman of the Legal Council of the Office of the Council of Ministers and Coordinator of the training course, thanked the Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth for initiating the orientation and directing the training. And thank you to Dr. Say Borey, an honorary speaker full of ability and experience who volunteered to share knowledge and experience to this training.
Under the initiative of Mr. Vongsey Visoth, this training course is the fifth time that the Legal Council of the Council of Ministers has organized such a training course after the establishment of the Royal Government of the seventh mandate to build and strengthen human resource capacity within the framework. The entire Office of the Council of Ministers, as well as in various ministries, institutions and universities.
The first three training sessions were presented by Dr. Sok Siphana, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions, and the fourth and fifth sessions were presented by Dr. Say Borey, Government Advisor and Legal Advisor.
The Office of the Council of Ministers will organize training courses on more important topics to ensure that the performance of all leaders and officials is effective, efficient and productive to meet the requests and needs of their respective units. .
According to the Kremlin, Putin wants former Defense Minister Sergei Shoigu to become an influential Secretary of State in the Russian National Security Adviser, responsible for the defense industry. Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet and Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chanmony Support the Treatment of Serious Heart Cancer by Nuth Nareth, Professor of the Royal University of Agriculture and Provide Scholarships to Their Two Daughters
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of May 14, 2024, Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chanmony met and gave some money to Ms. Ly Von That, wife of Dr. Nuth Nareth, Professor of Royal University of Agriculture, who has severe heart cancer. Being treated abroad to alleviate the burden of the family.
At the same time, Samdech Prime Minister and Lok Chumteav Bandith also provided scholarships to her two daughters to get education, knowledge and opportunities for further study.
Please be informed that Mr. Nuth Nareth, who was an outstanding student from an early age, struggled to study until he became an active officer and continued his PhD in Agricultural Science in Japan, fell ill with advanced heart cancer, a rare disease. He is currently recovering in Thailand, where he needs a lot of money for treatment.
Nuth Nareth, 39, head of the department of the Faculty of Agricultural Engineering at the Royal University of Agriculture, fell ill in August 2023 after studying in Costa Rica, Latin America for about two months. As his condition did not improve, his family was sent to Thailand for treatment and treatment. During a month and a half of treatment, Thailand has already undergone four surgeries to remove fluid from the lungs and heart.
Ly Montha, Nuth Nareth's wife, said it had been nine months since her husband had been diagnosed with serious heart cancer and had spent a lot of money on treatment. He is currently receiving treatment in Thailand and awaiting chemotherapy.
She said doctors required three chemotherapy injections at a time, at a cost of about $ 3,500, a large amount, and her family was unable to afford treatment.
Nuth Nareth's illness has severely affected his family's livelihood, as she is currently seven months pregnant and has two young children in her care, while she is unable to go to work. Business.
She requested the philanthropists and the head of the Royal Government to provide as much money as possible to continue to treat Mr. Nuth Nareth so that he can come to work to help train students in the field of agriculture.
She mentioned that Mr. Nuth Nareth is an official and an active teacher who has dedicated his energy and time to work and teach students to gain knowledge related to agriculture.
Please be informed that Mr. Nuth Nareth has a background as an excellent student from primary to high school. When he came to study in higher education, he was still an outstanding student who received a series of scholarships to study abroad, such as Thailand, Israel and Japan.
After graduating from General Education in Siem Reap, Nuth Nareth went on to study higher education between 2005 and 2009. He holds a Bachelor of Science in Technology and Agricultural Management from the Royal University of Agriculture. In 2007-2008, he also attended a diploma course in Israel.
From 2011 to 2013, he studied abroad and completed a master's degree from Khon Kaen University, Thailand. From 2018 to 2023, he holds a PhD in Agricultural Science from the University of Agriculture, Tokyo, Japan.
