Netanyahu says nearly half of Gaza's dead are Hamas fighters
JERUSALEM (Reuters) - Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said in a podcast that nearly half of the Gaza war deaths were from Hamas fighters, while maintaining the position that the civilian death toll was lower. Figures provided by Gaza officials. This is according to a release by the AFP news agency.
At least 35,091 people have been killed in the more than seven-month war between Israel and Hamas, according to Gaza health officials. But in a podcast interview on Sunday this weekend, Netanyahu claimed that the death toll in the Gaza Strip was about 30,000, and that nearly half of those killed were Hamas militants.
