(Phnom Penh): Five activists of the Candlelight Party and the Khmer Will have decided to leave their old party to join the Cambodian People's Party. The decision to change the political life of the opposition to join the ruling party because they lost faith in the leadership of the conflicting and divided opposition, especially not in the spirit of national interests.
Ms. Kang Mao said she had been involved in political activities with the opposition for many years. But so far, she has lost faith in the leadership of the party leadership, which has led to a series of internal divisions and conflicts.
In addition, the party leadership did not act in accordance with the principles and spirit that always claim to uphold the national interest.
While expressing dissatisfaction with the opposition party she used to live with, Ms. Kang Mao also highlighted the advantages of the Cambodian People's Party, which led her to decide to live with. Ms. Kang Mao expressed her view that the Cambodian People's Party, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has a clear policy for both party leadership and national leadership.
Proper leadership has made the CPP stronger as a strong support in nation building and development. In addition, through its role as the leader of the Royal Government, the Cambodian People's Party has set out a clear policy to build and develop the nation for continuous progress.
Ms. Kang Mao called on all members of the opposition party to wake up and join the nation-building with the Cambodian People's Party.
