Senior Minister Ieng Moly Holds a Meeting on HIV / AIDS Response on Health
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Ieng Moly, President of the National AIDS Authority, opens a meeting on HIV / AIDS response on health on May 13, 2024 at the National AIDS Authority. The meeting was attended by the working group of the AIDS Committee of the Ministry of Health, led by Mr. Ung Phirun, Chairman of the Committee of the Ministry of Health.
The main objectives of this meeting are as follows:
First, Cambodia's HIV / AIDS Achievements in the Health Sector; Second, Examine the Functionality of the Joint System in Response to HIV; Sustainable AIDS programs in the health sector.
Senior Minister Ieng Moly, President of the National Authority, praised the Ministry of Health for its efforts to participate in the implementation of the HIV response in the past. On this occasion, the Senior Minister also clarified the roles and responsibilities of the National AIDS Authority in accordance with Sub-Decree No. 109. Subsequently, the Senior Minister, the Chairman of the meeting, allowed the following presentation:
* Presentation on the Physical Response of HIV and AIDS by Dr. Tea Phala, Deputy Director of the National AIDS Authority, highlighted: the message and causes of the HIV response, the involvement of funding from various sources and the prioritization of issues, as well as the dynamic integration. He also outlined health coordination measures to achieve the goal of responding to HIV.
Ung Phirun, chairman of the AIDS Committee, said at the meeting that all institutions under the Ministry should cooperate with national authorities to monitor and implement the HIV response. The Ministry's AIDS Committee may report to the National Authority quarterly.
