Spokesman: "Golden Dragon" exercise between Cambodian and Chinese troops does not threaten any country, Cambodia welcomes friendly countries who wish to conduct exercises but must respect Cambodia's rights
(Phnom Penh): Major General Thong Solimo, Spokesman of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, reaffirmed that the 6th Golden Dragon Exercise 2024 between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army on Cambodian territory is not intended to intimidate. Or harm any country. Cambodia always welcomes friendly countries that wish to conduct exercises but must respect Cambodia's rights.
The 6th Golden Dragon Exercise will be held under the theme "Joint Counter-Terrorism Operation and Humanitarian Work", which will run for 14 days from 16 to 30 May 2024, with the participation of the Army and the Army. Cambodian waters, for the army, will be held at the Gendarmerie Training Center in Chrak Kov village, Peam commune, Samaki Meanchey district, Kampong Chhnang province, and the sea exercise will be held in Sihanoukville.
Speaking at a press conference on the afternoon of May 13, 2024, Major General Thong Solimo stated: "The exercise between the Cambodian Army and the Chinese People's Liberation Army is based on the cooperation of the two countries." "Every year, as we have done five times to learn from each other, strengthen security and prevent terrorism, so this exercise is not intended to threaten or harm any country."
Meanwhile, a spokesman for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) said that in addition to the Golden Dragon exercise with the Chinese People's Liberation Army, the Cambodian Army will also hold joint exercises with the Lao and Vietnamese armies on disaster relief.
