(Mondulkiri): A doctor was shot dead by an AK 47 assault rifle in the health room of Andong Latheung, and the bullet hit another 6-year-old child, injuring him. This incident happened at midnight on May 12, 2024 in Andong Kraloeng village, Sen Monorom commune, Oreang district, Mondulkiri province.
According to reports, the gunman tried to shoot himself in the back, but the bullet did not explode. The gunman had a wife and children, but was in love with the victim, before the shooting was heard arguing between the perpetrator and the victim.
Hak Tith Rithivong, O'Raing District Police Inspector, said that the gunman used an AK-47 assault rifle in the middle of the head, piercing the spine, and the bullet bounced off another girl, injuring her child. The victim's girl.
According to the police, the victim, Kep Keo Kanika, 38, a doctor, went to Andong Kraloeng village, Sen Monorom commune, Oreang district (died immediately), while his other daughter, Chou Sana, was injured. 6 years. Separately, the gunman named Sokha Nuth, 41 years old, is a farmer.
