Four Injured in Explosive Remnants of War in Chhnuk Trou Commune, Boribo District
(Kampong Chhnang): Four people were seriously and lightly injured in the explosion of a bomb left over from the war, an unknown type of bullet that the victim picked up from the river and threw a toy that caused the bomb to explode Up.
The above incident happened at 4:00 pm on May 11, 2024 at Koh Mono in Chhnuk Trou village, Chhnuk Trou commune, Baribo district, Kampong Chhnang province.
Mr. Cheng Chandorna, Governor of Baribo District, said on May 12, 2024 that the four victims were named Sen Sary, male, 23 years old, seriously injured Sen Pu Kao, male, 43 years old. Sen Malich, a 10-year-old boy, was seriously injured and another child, just over a year old, was slightly injured. All victims are Khmer Muslims living in Chhnuk Trou village, Chhnuk Trou commune, Baribo district, Kampong Chhnang province.
After the accident, with the care of the Governor of Kampong Chhnang, he ordered the ambulance of the Baribo District Referral Hospital to transport the victim to the hospital immediately. Doctors and specialized police forces, in cooperation with the CMAC, arrived at the scene to inspect the scene for any unexploded ordnance.
