(Banteay Meanchey): An old man took an old DK75 bomb left over from the war, cut it into pieces to make a cow bell, and exploded shards, killing all of them on the afternoon of the 12th of this month. May 2024 at the victim's house in Trang village, Phnom Dey commune, Phnom Srok district, Banteay Meanchey province.
Phnom Srok District Police said that on the day of the incident, the victim, 45-year-old Prang Bis, a resident of Trang Village, Phnom Dey Commune, Phnom Srok District, Banteay Meanchey Province, took an unexploded ordnance (DK75). He went to plow the field and found it old and kept it under the barn for more than a year without reporting it to the authorities.
Then, on May 12, 2024, the victim took the unexploded ordnance (DK75) that he had hidden and split it into two pieces for the purpose of processing it into cow bells. After the explosion, the explosion caused The pieces of nuts are scraped off and die instantly. Separately, the wife was busy going to the plantation and the first child was sleeping on the house, the second child was sitting watching his father, more than 10 meters away, but he was not injured.
After the incident, police and officers arrived at the scene to search for the bomb, said that the unexploded ordnance, although buried in the ground left over from the war, can still explode. .
Police and professional officers, after making a report, handed over the body to the family for a traditional ceremony.
