Agriculture Minister: Donation of a pair of Lao elephants will contribute to increase the number of domestic elephants and replace the older domestic elephants
(Takeo): The Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Dith Tina, said that the donation of a pair of Lao elephants will contribute to increasing the number of domestic elephants, with both elephants at a young age being able to reproduce and replace domestic elephants. Which is getting older because Cambodia does not allow the capture of wild elephants.
Dith Tina said elephants are currently present in the northern highlands and the Cardamom Mountains, with an estimated 400-600 wild elephants and 75 domestic elephants in the area. Cambodia.
He added that Cambodia has also prepared a 10-year plan for elephant conservation activities (2020-2029), setting out strategic actions to reduce the threat to the lives of elephants, in cooperation with conservation partners. Elephant conservation in Cambodia has achieved remarkable results.
Linkham DOUANGSAVANH added that the precious gift of a pair of elephants will further strengthen the traditional solidarity and symbolize the close and lasting cooperation between the two countries, especially in the care of the species. Suffering and contributing to environmental education to the public of both countries, scientific research, tourism and elephant conservation outside the region.
In addition, in the next 10-12 years, the reproduction of this pair of elephants will help increase the number of elephants in the protected park and "Tamao" botanical park, which reflects the cooperation in Promote the care and prosperity of domestic elephants.
