Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie Sends Two Suspects to Court Over Drug Trafficking Case
(Banteay Meanchey): The Anti-Drug Office of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie on May 12, 2024, sent two suspects along with drug exhibits to the Provincial Court for legal proceedings.
It should be noted that at 18:00 on May 10, 2024, the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie Local Force led by Brigadier General Nuon Ninaro, the Commander of the Poipet Municipal Gendarmerie, conducted an operation to crack down on illegal trafficking. Drugs at the EDM Entertainment Club in Samaki Meanchey Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City, arrested 2 suspects, including:
First: Name: Thorn Limhong, alias Sna, Male, 32 years old, Nationality: Khmer, Occupation: Electrician, Present address: Kbal Spean 1 Village, Sangkat O'Chrov, Poipet City. Current residence: Nimit 1 village, Sangkat Nimit, Poipet city.
Colonel Nuon Ninaro, Commander of the Municipal Gendarmerie Base, said that prior to the crackdown, the Municipal Gendarmerie had received information from residents that there was a case of illegal drug trafficking in front of the EDM Entertainment Club. .
Immediately, the force went down to the scene and found two suspects riding a motorcycle. On suspicion, the force detained, interrogated and inspected the two suspects and found drugs in the body of the suspect. Thorn Lim Hong called Sna. The name Ly Udom is called Dom (no evidence). The detention force then confiscated the exhibits and brought them to the Municipal Gendarmerie Base for processing.
After being arrested and interrogated, the suspects confessed that they had actually bought drugs to sell. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the Municipal Gendarmerie has prepared a case file and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Colonel Chea Dara, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of anti-drug work, said that the crackdown was also authorized by Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie and coordinated the procedure. From Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court.
