Mr. Neth Pheaktra: The Ministry of Information continues to participate in achieving the four basic rights of children in the cause of creating human resources with knowledge, morality, virtue, behavior and ethics.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, stated that the Ministry of Information is committed to continuing to participate in achieving the four basic rights of children in the cause of creating human resources with knowledge, ethics, morality and ethics.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra's remarks were made on the occasion that he and his wife, Ms. Tuy Serey Ratanakneth Pheaktra, Honorary President of the Women's Association for Peace and Development, Ministry of Information Branch, presided over the opening of the 2024 Children's Music and Song Festival. On the afternoon of May 12, 2024 at Chaktomuk Mongkul Hall, Ministry of Information.
Minister Neth Pheaktra stated that the Children's Music and Song Festival organized by the Ministry of Information is an opportunity for boys and girls to express their talents and talents through the art of music and songs that are characteristic for children. Transforming content into education provides long-term useful knowledge for life skills, meaning that education is linked to the art of music.
In line with the above theme, the images and content of the Children's Music and Song Festival, the Ministry of Information Award, which has been organized from 2012 to this year, is a joint commitment of the five specialized working groups, the General Department and the Working Group for Children. The Ministry of Information, as a staff, has been actively involved in the field of children.
The Minister commended the leadership, especially Ms. Chanthy and her team for initiating and re-organizing the Children's Music and Song Festival, and thanked Mr. Huot Kheang Veng for his efforts to seek additional financial support. From various philanthropists to support the 2024 Children's Music and Song Festival in response to the request of the Ministry in addition to the supported national budget.
The Minister would like to express his deep gratitude to the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, National Council of Cambodia for Children, Director General, Director General, Teachers from public and private schools throughout Cambodia for their efforts in the process. Organize and participate in the festival now.
On this happy occasion, the Minister of Information would like to wish all the boys and girls who came to participate in the success of their respective abilities.
The 2024 Children's Music and Song Festival, with a total of 34 groups of public and private schools in the capital-province, equal to 200 children, will show their talents to become the winners of the Ministry of Information, which will be announced at the closing ceremony on May 27, 2004
