The following is the Royal Decree: Cambodia celebrates Migratory Bird Day, focusing on the importance of insects for birds
(Pursat): The Ministry of Environment has organized the World Migratory Bird Day 2024 under the theme "Insect protection is bird protection" to raise awareness of the importance of wetlands and raise awareness among the public to participate in bird conservation in Pursat Province.
Khvay Atiya, a spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, said the Migratory Bird Day had been launched since 2006 and was an annual outreach campaign to conserve migratory birds and their habitats. .
Every year in the second week of May, around the world, public events such as bird forums, bird education programs, bird pictures exhibitions, live bird surveys and other activities are held every year in the second week of May. More. This year, Migratory Bird Day focuses on the importance of insects, the main food of migratory birds.
"Disruption and loss of insects in the breeding and spawning grounds threatens the well-being and survival of the birds," he added. Some of the reasons that have threatened the migration and reproduction of birds of these species are the loss of insect habitats such as pastures, the use of pesticides to protect crops from pests.
Through this, the Ministry of Environment has launched a campaign to provide and plant at least 1 million trees per year from 2024. The Ministry will organize a promotion ceremony and provide seedlings to the public for free under the theme "Green Sprouts" from July 10-16, 2024 in front of the Ministry of Environment.
