Analysis: Sino-Hungarian relations reach the best stage in history
BEIJING, May 8 (Xinhua) - Chinese President Xi Jinping paid a state visit to Hungary from May 8 to 10. During the visit, the leaders of the two countries issued a joint statement announcing the expansion of China-Hungary relations from a comprehensive strategic partnership to a comprehensive strategic partnership under all circumstances.
This year marks the 75th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations between China and Hungary. For the past 75 years, the two countries have maintained mutual understanding, equality, trust and mutual assistance, and won-win cooperation. China-Hungary relations have reached the best stage in history, should raise the level of bilateral relations to another level and enrich the cooperation between the two countries.
