It should be informed that this week, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training organized a visit of 10 journalists to Kampong Speu Provincial Polytechnic Institute, a school to implement vocational training programs for young people from poor and vulnerable families. At risk of 1.5 million people, the media also interviewed the director of the institute, Mr. Kem Chakny, teachers and students who learn some technical skills.
Regarding the vocational training program for the 1.5 million poor and vulnerable families, Mr. Kem Chakny stated that in the first step according to the plan of the institute, only 390 students were selected, but there were actually students. Up to 448 students (14% over plan) are currently receiving training in various skills.
Mr. Kem Chakny Institute Director confirmed that in the second phase, Kampong Speu Polytechnic Institute will recruit 570 students so that they can come and receive vocational training for everyone.
Ministry of Labor spokesman Kata On also confirmed that after the success of the first phase, the ministry is also preparing to implement the second phase, which plans to accept more than 30,000 students, as well as add some professional skills. But there are trainers, teaching materials and high demand in the job market.
