(Foreign): Many events have taken place in the history of the world, including the event that the European powers colonized the kingdoms in Asia is also a turning point in history, but do you know which colonies? Who arrived in Asia first?
In 1565, the Spanish Empire raised a navy to conquer the Cebu Empire and later established the capital Manila in 1571 under Spanish rule.
Dutch troops made the long voyage by sea to Japan in 1600 AD. About 19 years later, the Dutch seized the capital, Jakarta, or Jakarta, from the Javanese Muslim kingdom and renamed the city Jakarta "Pattavia".
The presence of these three colonial armies did not seem to be very competitive and did not go deep into the kingdoms on the mainland. Most of their location is along the coast. It was not until the arrival of British and French troops that arrived in Asia later in the 18th century that colonial events on the continent began to escalate.
Meanwhile, French troops arrived in Indochina in 1858 and colonized Tonkin, Annam, Cochinchina (Kampuchea Krom), Cambodia, as far as Laos and parts of China.
Before World War I, India and Southeast Asia fell under the yoke of European power almost entirely, with the exception of Siam, which was able to escape the clutches of the West thanks to the agreement of Britain and France. Together in 1896, leaving this empire as a buffer zone or white zone between the colonies of the two powers.
