Tycoon Try Pheap was ordered by the King to be given the title of "Duke"
(Phnom Penh): Oknha Try Pheap, General Director of Try Pheap Group, was ordered by His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, to be given the title of "Oknha".
This Royal Decree conferring this title was signed by His Majesty the King on Friday, May 10, 2024.
Mr. Try Pheap was the eighth person to receive the royal favor of the King, ordering him to be given the title of "Duke".
It should be noted that on April 6, 2024, Mr. Oknha Try Pheap was appointed by the King to be an advisor to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate of Cambodia.
In addition, on April 19, Duke Try Pheap was appointed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen as his special envoy. Permanent Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth: Cambodia still believes in and adheres to the policy of multilateralism and open policy
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Deputy Prime Minister in charge of the Office of the Council of Ministers, said that Cambodia still believes in and adheres to the policy of multilateralism and open policy.
This statement was made on the occasion of his visit as a representative of His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia at the opening ceremony of "Cambodia International Trade Fair 2024" on the morning of May 10, 2024 with the participation of Mrs. Cham Nimmol, Minister of Commerce, as well as many well-known national and international investors.
In addition to the business aspect, Mr. Vongsey Visoth highlighted the concept that trade and investment must be linked, and also expressed the hope that the exhibition will also bring new investment opportunities in Cambodia by bringing Technology, knowledge, business knowledge and new skills to add value and especially create jobs for people and support national economic growth.
The Permanent Deputy Prime Minister affirmed that the Royal Government of Cambodia still believes in and adheres to the policy of multilateralism and open policy in promoting trade and investment, despite the world facing many uncertainties. Both in terms of politics, economy, finance and society due to geopolitical changes, the fragmentation of the world economic system and trade.
In the above context, the Royal Government of Cambodia, the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, under the leadership of His Majesty the King Hun Manet, has launched the first phase of the Pentagon Strategy for Employment Growth, Equity, Efficiency and Sustainability aimed at protecting, preserving and accumulating national achievements. Raise national prestige, boost economic growth, and build the foundation to achieve high-middle-income status by 2030 and high-income country by 2050.
In addition, Mr. Vongsey Visoth also mentioned the drastic measures packaged by the Prime Minister at the 19th Royal Government-Private Sector Forum to address the challenges and concerns of the private sector and show that Cambodia has Ready to receive more new investors and investments.
At the same time, Mr. Vongsey Visoth also highlighted the Royal Government's efforts to develop and ensure economic growth, as well as sharing to ensure the economic structure.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Vongsey Visoth, Cambodia's economy is projected to grow at around 6% in 2024 and in 2025. In fact, in the first quarter of 2024, the trade volume increased significantly by 11.9% compared to the same period in 2023.
