The following is the announcement of the Administrative Regulator: Quentum Charitable Organization provides a school building to Prey Top Primary School in Chhuk District, Kampot Province.
(Kampot): Mr. Ung Kongkea, Representative of Quentum Charity Organization, led the delegation to attend the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of a new school building in Prey Top Primary School, Boeung Nimol Commune, Chhuk District, Kampot Province.
The groundbreaking ceremony was held on the morning of May 10, 2024, presided over by Mr. Khieu Rithiphon, Deputy Governor of Kampot Province, on behalf of Mr. Mao Thanin, Governor of Kampot Provincial Board of Governors, with the participation of monks, district governor, commune chief, director. The school is full of teachers, students and parents.
The new school building, donated by Quentum Charity, has a size of 390 square meters, a four-room brick and tile building, planned to be built in three months at a cost of more than 50,000 US dollars.
Mr. Ibora, Principal of Prey Top Primary School and student guardian, was very happy. They say that after receiving a school building as a precious gift from Samdech Ta and Samdech Yeay in 1997, this poor school has never received another new school building, while the number of students Increases every year.
Some grandparents even said that today, even the sky turned green to join in the joy of opening the construction site of our new school.
According to the principal, today Prey Top Primary School has a total of 310 students divided into 7 classes from kindergarten to 6th grade under the tutelage of 6 teachers.
Mr. Ung Kongkea said that his organization is pleased to have contributed to the provision of school buildings to the children of people in rural areas.
He learned that Prey Top Primary School has a large number of students, but only two classrooms, so teachers have to teach them in three shifts, unlike the general school, he understands the difficulties of teachers and students. Each person contributes $ 10-20 until they build this school building for Prey Top Primary School today.
He encourages children to study hard to become human resources to participate in building society in the future.
Mr. Khieu Rithiphorn welcomed and thanked the Quantum delegation for donating money for the construction of a new school building for Prey Top Primary School.
He even prepared a delicious lunch for the Quantum Charity delegation at his farm.
He said that Kampot has great potential in terms of economy and tourism, with Kampot turmeric, Kampot pepper, which is a destination, including yellow bananas, which are exported to the Chinese market. In the near future, Kampot province will inaugurate the use of more deep-water ports, which will boost the export-import trade to grow even more.
