Kep Provincial Administration Celebrates 138th Anniversary of International Labor Day May 1
(Kep): Dr. Som Piseth, Governor of Kep Province, led more than 300 government officials, forces, authorities, representatives of employers, workers in various enterprises in Kep province to celebrate the 138th anniversary of International Labor Day on May 1, 2024. The theme "An enterprise is a peaceful community" organized by the Department of Labor and Vocational Training of Kep Province on May 9, 204 at the Kep Provincial Hall.
Ms. Samorn, Director of the Department of Labor and Vocational Training of Kep Province, stated that May 1 International Labor Day is a historical event of the International Workers' Movement, which began in 1886 with the aim of improving the working conditions and living conditions of workers. .
In particular, in Cambodia, International Labor Day, May 1 has been celebrated every year since 1979, and until now, the Royal Government of Cambodia, with His Excellency Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has designated May 1 as a Labor Day for Cambodian workers and It is a public holiday for all workers, such as national holidays, traditional festivals and international holidays.
On that occasion, Mr. Som Piseth, Governor of Cambodia, read out a message from Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia on the occasion of the 138th Anniversary of International Labor Day, May 1, 2024. With all workers, employers and compatriots.
At the same time, the provincial governor also praised the Department of Labor and Vocational Training, which has cooperated well with relevant institutions to regularly disseminate education to employers, employees, workers to understand the law on labor, prevent labor disputes and create Build mutual understanding in professional relations between all stakeholders.
He advised people to stay away from drugs and gambling of all kinds, strive to earn a living, improve living standards and strengthen professional skills, because work is a key factor in determining the standard of living and an effective way to cut. Reduce poverty. On that occasion, the provincial governor presented a souvenir with a sarong and some money to all participants.
