Head of the Department of Agricultural Engineering of the Royal University of Agriculture suffers from severe heart cancer, lack of access to treatment, calls for support
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Nuth Nareth, who was an outstanding student from an early age, struggled to study until he became an active officer and continued his PhD in Agricultural Science in Japan, fell ill with severe heart cancer, a rare disease. He is currently recovering in Thailand, where he needs a lot of money to treat the disease.
At the age of 39, Nuth Nareth is the Head of the Department of Agricultural Engineering at the Royal University of Agriculture. He fell ill in August 2023 after studying in Costa Rica, Latin America for about two months. As his condition did not improve, his family was sent to Thailand for treatment and treatment. During a month and a half of treatment, Thailand has already undergone four surgeries to remove fluid from the lungs and heart.
Ly Montha, Nut Nareth's wife, said it had been nine months since her husband had been diagnosed with serious heart cancer and had spent a lot of money on treatment. He is currently receiving treatment in Thailand and awaiting chemotherapy.
"Currently, we are short of funds for treatment because we have been receiving treatment for a long time and now we need to continue to receive chemotherapy," she added. "Doctors say he has a rare disease and will continue to receive chemotherapy and follow-up."
She mentioned that Mr. Nuth Nareth is an official and an active teacher who has dedicated his energy and time to work and teach students to gain knowledge related to agriculture.
Please be informed that Mr. Nuth Nareth has a background as an excellent student from primary to high school. When he came to study in higher education, he was still an outstanding student who received a series of scholarships to study abroad, such as Thailand, Israel and Japan.
