Mr. Neth Pheaktra added that this children's music and song festival was created by the previous generation of leaders, especially thanks to Mr. Khieu Kanharith, former Minister of Information, and Ms. Chanthy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Information, for organizing this event. Preserve the legacy of old leaders established to provide significant benefits for children.
At the same time, the Minister of Information also thanked the philanthropists who have supported and sponsored the 2024 Children's Music and Song Festival, including: Duke Kith Meng and Lok Chumteav Neak Oknha Mao Chamnan, Oknha Pung Kheav Se and Lok Chumteav, Duke Leang Khun and Lok Chumteav, Duke Sam Ang Vattanak, Duke Sok Chamroeun and Lok Chumteav, Duke Sear Rithy, Metfone and other philanthropists.
CCHR Spokesperson It is necessary to explain the following:
First, the Universal Periodic Review (UPR) mechanism is a mechanism that aims to share best practices, best experiences and challenges, or as a platform for mutual learning. As a member of the United Nations in the sense of making global progress in the field of human rights. That is, it is not a platform for attacking, criticizing, pressuring or degrading human rights.
Third, all recommendations made by countries to Cambodia, Cambodia, as a member of the United Nations, as a sovereign state, has the full right to decide which recommendations to adopt and which to note. On the other hand, the total number of recommendations that Cambodia has received is small compared to the number of recommendations that many major democracies have received in this UPR mechanism.
Fourthly, one-sided dissemination of information and only the recommendations of a small number of countries whose political character does not reflect the facts and has no clear basis are malicious intentions that confuse the people. People to the Royal Government of Cambodia for the promotion and protection of human rights.
For example, in all the recommendations given by Australia, also praised the progress of LGBT rights and called on Cambodia to continue this positive progress and praised Japan for renewing the MoU. Together with the OHCHR in Cambodia, as well as the progress on the promotion of socio-economic rights and vulnerable groups is not mentioned in the reports of some media outlets criticizing the Royal Government.
Fifth, in order to have a comprehensive basis, journalists should clearly understand the UPR mechanism and monitor or research the process of reviewing the UPR report of major democracies, whether representatives of other countries raised issues at the forum. What about the human rights situation in their country?
Sixth, Cambodia welcomes constructive criticism from all quarters, but any criticism or comment that embodies political intentions, wants a window of honor, does not reflect the reality of Cambodia, or seeks to destroy the hard-won peace and Contrary to the principles set out in the UN Charter, Cambodia is unacceptable and must take all possible measures to prevent it.
And 7: Spokesperson of CCHR Request units and media to disseminate information in a comprehensive and balanced manner, that is, to respect professional ethics in order to demonstrate integrity, neutrality and respect for the public's right to information. Representatives of the family of Mr. Chiao Tai sent a message thanking the leadership for sending a message of condolences
