Prime Minister Hun Manet Vows to Increase Attraction to New Investors in Cambodia and Establish an Effective Private Sector Working Group (Video inside) (Phnom Penh) New investors in Cambodia will set up effective working groups to address private sector challenges.
He said this on the occasion of presiding over the official opening of the Federation of Cambodian Investors Association and a solidarity meal at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center on the afternoon of May 9, 2024.
He said that in order to attract more new investment, the Royal Government must make sure that all existing investors in Cambodia grow to be able to attract more newcomers. To achieve this, it is necessary to increase the positive factors and reduce the negative factors.
Samdech said that in order to increase the positive factors, it is done through the introduction of policies, incentives, favors and budgets to support key areas that the Royal Government has already done through the introduction. Government intervention policy in this mandate.
"We have reformed the work, reduced the complexity of procedures, reduced the number of bureaucrats, reduced the use of technology to facilitate employment and the private sector," he added.
"These settlement mechanisms are a step in attracting new investors to invest in Cambodia," he said.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that in order to ensure compliance, close cooperation between the private sector and the Royal Government is required to build mutual trust in both the private and private sectors. Both state institutions and state institutions.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia said, "In business, as long as the private sector joins the Royal Government, it is necessary to work together to strengthen compliance, which means that everyone must unite to implement the principles we have agreed to "Let us compete tirelessly, can easily plan, build state-to-state trust between the private sector and the private sector."
According to Hun Manet, for the Association to be established, when the common principles are set, all members must apply in accordance with the rules to ensure the sustainability of the association. Because otherwise, the association will definitely fall apart.
Samdech Hun Sen also claimed that if an association of all members followed at the same time, those who followed would be easier to carry out their duties because there was a clear standard. He compared the implementation and respect of compliance with the traffic law to facilitate travel together to ensure no traffic accidents.
At this point of conformity, Samdech President Hun Manet noted that in the past, just hearing the word compliance, investors seem to express concern and even consider state institutions like cats waiting to catch mice, that is, state institutions must catch the private sector. Only.
The head of the Royal Government explained that in order to ensure the sustainability of doing business, not only state institutions must be held accountable, but also state institutions must play a supporting role, not just fines. The president does not want to hear the word "state" and "park" but instead wants a partnership between state institutions and the private sector to complement each other.
Hun Manet stressed that the private sector and public institutions must work together to create an attractive and competitive investment environment and turn Cambodia into a country where investors want to invest in order to promote the private sector. Further progress.
AMRO commends Cambodia for maintaining macroeconomic and financial stability despite the global economic situation and the region facing many challenges and risks
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Li Kouqing, Director of the ASEAN Plus Three Macroeconomic Research Bureau, praised Cambodia for continuing to maintain macroeconomic and financial stability, which has made a significant contribution to improving the public financial situation. Sustainability is strong despite the global economic situation and the region has been facing many challenges and risks.
Dr. Ly Kuching's speech was made on the occasion that he and his colleagues of the Mission of the ASEAN Plus Three Macroeconomic Research Bureau paid a courtesy call and discussed with Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Economy and Finance. On the morning of May 9, 2024 at the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
On that occasion, Dr. Li Kuoching thanked for the cooperation of Cambodia and expressed his high appreciation to the Royal Government of Cambodia for maintaining macroeconomic and financial stability. Cambodia's Economic Situation in 2023 Economic growth is estimated at around 5%, which is good growth, despite the global and regional economic situation has been facing many challenges and risks.
For 2024, the Cambodian economy will continue to maintain a good growth momentum in anticipation of better global and regional economic growth, which will continue to support the export sector, especially the garment and non-garment industries, while tourism will continue. The upward trend.
He stressed that good economic growth in 2023 and 2024 has contributed significantly to improving the public financial situation to be sustainable, strong and increase the space for necessary interventions while the external position (External Position). Also improved. This trend will continue to enable Cambodia to achieve better growth for 2025 and in the medium term.
With a warm welcome to the AMRO team, Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth highlighted the importance of AMRO's annual mission in assessing the macroeconomic, financial and public financial situation in Cambodia, providing good policy recommendations for The Royal Government considers.
Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet announces efforts to help Cambodian investors to grow and maintain competitive excellence (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet has vowed to do his best to Make Cambodian investors more competitive and successful by helping Cambodian investors grow and maintain their competitive advantage.
His Excellency Hun Manet said this on May 9, 2024, on the occasion of presiding over the official opening of the Federation of Cambodian Investors Association and Solidarity Dinner.
The Federation of Cambodian Investors Association was established with the aim of bringing together the components of each association together into a large nursery, strengthening and expanding activities to attract foreign investors from all countries. Royal Government of Cambodia.
"I, as the head of the Royal Government, have set out the principles and are committed to doing my best to make investors in Cambodia more competitive and more successful," he said. "Furthermore."
Samdech Hun Sen added that Cambodia has put forward programs and policies to attract more through the maintenance of the old, expand the new as a way to solve problems in a timely manner and further improve. But let the private sector be a partner of the Royal Government of Cambodia in promoting the economy, especially the successful development of the business sector in Cambodia.
At the same time, Samdech Hun Sen expressed his gratitude to all investors, both investors in Cambodia and investors from abroad for the decision to invest in Cambodia and trust in Cambodia.
He stressed that these investment projects are the result of the efforts of the Royal Government and the private sector to jointly attract investors to Cambodia, which he has always said "walking around" in the past.
He added that on the evening of May 8, 2024, he had just signed the agreement on 14 investment projects with an investment of 480 million dollars, as a result of which Cambodia received and will continue to do so.
The Prime Minister's speech was made on the occasion of presiding over the official opening of the Cambodian Federation of Investors and Solidarity Dinner at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center on the afternoon of May 9, 2024.
The Prime Minister said, "This is what we have worked together to promote Cambodia, we together to build trust from investors, both existing and new investors, and this is an achievement in "The eight months that the Royal Government has set out are the results on the ground for our people."
He added that Cambodia's investment approach is to use two approaches to keep the old and expand the new, while attracting new investment to invest in Cambodia, the Royal Government has taken action to facilitate existing investment. The ability to continue to succeed and expand its capabilities further, as the Khmer word says, "Keep five sparrows in your hand is better than 20 sparrows in the forest and take a dove to catch a dove in the forest."
Ministry of Labor Spokesman: CATU Promotion's Old Case
(Phnom Penh): The Office of the Spokesperson of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on the evening of May 9 highlighted that the case disseminated by the Cambodian Confederation of Trade Unions (CATU) led by Ms. Yang Sophorn is an old case that has occurred since August 2020. This was confirmed on the official Facebook page of Mr. Sun Mesa, the second deputy spokesman of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on May 9, 2024.
According to the spokesperson, for May 9, 2024, traffic police nationwide inspected and fined a total of 2,865 vehicles, including 2,211 motorcycles and 652 vehicles.
Noted offenses for motorcycles include: drunken helmets, fire / badges, etc. In particular, the vehicles include: heavy transport, drunkenness, speeding, drunken driving, processing without a driver's license, and license plates.
It should be noted that for May 9, 2024, there were 10 traffic accidents throughout Cambodia, in which 5 people were killed and 7 people were injured (5 people were seriously injured). In 9 days, there were 71 traffic accidents, resulting in 45 deaths, 57 injuries (37 serious injuries).
