(Phnom Penh): From June 1 to November 30, 2024, with only about three weeks left, the tax administration will start collecting taxes on transportation for 2024. This is according to the weekly newsletter of the General Department of Taxation.
Transportation tax is an annual tax that is applied to the means of transportation in the Kingdom of Cambodia, both land and water, such as: ships, ferries, boats, ferries, cars, locomotives, trailers, semi-trailers, trailers, motorcycles, tricycles, tractors and machinery. Approximately and so on.
* Road: Must include information about the year of manufacture, cylinder size or total weight, while the means of processing is taxed according to the type of vehicle * Waterway: must include information on horsepower or total weight or length of Watercraft.
