Cambodia-China Friendship Radio The Minister of Information supports the activities of content creators and independent adventurers in developing a charity cycling program to raise funds for Cambodian children at Angkor Hospital for Children.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheakdra, Minister of Information, supported the activities of Mr. Tev Dararith, Content Creator and Independent Adventurer, in establishing a charity cycling program to raise funds for Cambodian children at Angkor Hospital for Children, which is planned to Departing from June 2024 to June 2025, passing through countries in Asia to some countries in Europe.
Mr. Neth Pheakdra has supported the charitable activities in this charity cycling program, and the Ministry of Information, which has the state media, will continue to promote the activities of Mr. Tev Dararith during the cycling trip to raise funds in any country or destination. Somewhere to show action, pictures, videos, those files.
The Minister of Information stated that this support focuses on two main points, the first point is to encourage young people to do humanitarian activities, which is to contribute both physical and mental strength to help Cambodian children. Point 2: Shows a young Cambodian man walking around the country from Asia to Europe, carrying the Cambodian flag to show our country, which is also a source of pride for our Cambodian nation.
"This is inextricably linked to the culture, civilization and customs of our country, which is a humanitarian action to help children," he said. This activity is also to spread the compassion of the Cambodian people to other people in the world. "This is a point that we need to support."
Mr. Neth Pheakdra also encouraged and advised Mr. Tev Dararith to take good care of his health while cycling across the long road to raise funds to help Cambodian children and succeed in this work.
Mr. Tev Dararith said that the creation of this charity cycling program project after he completed his cycling mission in the Southeast Asian region in 2023, which he still aims to continue the cycling process to raise funds to help children. Cambodia, who is being treated in hospital.
He confirmed that the cycling project is scheduled to take place in early June 2024 and is scheduled to depart from Siem Reap to countries in Asia such as: Laos, Thailand to Bangladesh, India, Pakistan, Iran and to the continent. In Europe, such as Turkey, the cycling process takes a whole year on the roads of 25 countries.
He added: "The purpose of cycling in these 25 countries is to raise $ 250,000 to donate to hospitals that are on a mission to save the lives of Cambodian children, especially children with cancer. Free. ”
Mr. Tev Dararith said that during the period 2022-2023, Angkor Hospital for Children was contacted in accordance with his intention to do so, so he took this opportunity to ride a bike in Asia. Southeast and fundraising from philanthropists to help the hospital.
He also stated, "This cycling trip, video production, photography, documentary, also contributed to society and raised money to help Cambodian children, and he called on philanthropists to support and donate money. More or less to help Cambodian children who are sick in the treatment and surgery in the hospital.
(Ratanakkiri): The authorities of Taveng District, Ratanakkiri Province have expressed their commitment to strengthen the participation of natural resources and environmental management in their geography.
It should be noted that the Ministry of Environment recently handed over 132 protected area maps to 21 provincial and 111 district administrations, reflecting another new achievement of the Ministry of Environment in implementing the Pentagon strategy. 1 of the Royal Government, the 7th mandate of the National Assembly and in accordance with the greenness and sustainability of the environmental chakra strategy in the context of environmental correctness.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of Environment, stated that the handing over of the protected area map to the sub-national administration is a testament to the implementation of decentralization and deconcentration policies, with the Ministry of Environment formulating policies and supporting the promotion of law enforcement. From the sub-national level.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth thanked for the participation of all stakeholders at the national and sub-national levels, strengthened cooperation and better implementation of all its roles and responsibilities, and participated in solving challenges with ownership. Responsibility for the management of natural resources and the conservation of biodiversity, especially to achieve great success for the Royal Government and the society of Cambodia.
The Minister urged the participation of all stakeholders and partners in accordance with the order of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, to strengthen the effective management of protected areas in accordance with the Environmental Chakra Strategy 2023-2028 to respond to climate change and Promote a green economy by promoting Cambodia's goal of "being a carbon neutral country with 60% forest cover by 2050."
It should be noted that protected areas have increased from 23 areas with a total area of about 3.3 million hectares, equivalent to 18% of the country's land area in 1993 to 73 areas with a total area of more than 7 million hectares. 40% of the country today.
Vietnam refuses to meet with top EU official on Russia sanctions as Putin may visit
(VOVworld) - Vietnamese Foreign Ministry officials have told the European Union (EU) that they can not hold a meeting next week with top EU officials in charge of sanctions on Russia, according to Vietnamese diplomats. No, while Hanoi is preparing for the possibility of a visit by Russian President Vladimir Putin. This was released by Reuters on Thursday, May 9, 2024.
Three other diplomatic sources also acknowledged the delay, with one revealing that Vietnam had asked for a meeting to be postponed to July. The other two sources said that the delay in meeting with senior EU officials was related to preparations for the possibility of Putin's visit to Vietnam, which could be adversely affected if any. An earlier visit by an EU official.
