This case was authorized by the President of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to Judge Mao Sina, the Judge in charge of Case No. 1497 dated September 29, 2020 of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court. During the trial, the judge had a close relationship with the plaintiff, Heng Pov, and the two of them were playing pong together.
He said that because the verdict was justified in the absence of him and his lawyer, he filed a complaint on July 5, 2022 to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court. Despite the objections, the proceedings were not processed and he was ordered to appeal to Judgment No. 407 "P" dated 26 April 2022.
The Court of Appeal then issued a judgment dated 18 January 2023, upholding Judgment No. 407 "P" dated 26 April 2022 of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court. The Supreme Court then upheld the Court of Appeal's ruling. The decision of the Court of Appeal and the Supreme Court because both courts are based on Judgment No. 407 "P" dated April 26, 2022 of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
According to the plaintiff, the evidence he presented to the court at the time of his dismissal did not take into account the evidence that the judge was involved in playing pong together. Establish intimacy with each other.
Due to such injustice, he decided to file a complaint to the Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Justice to seek the truth and to punish or punish individuals who have violated the law so that society has faith in the justice system of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
