Cambodia-China Friendship Radio Dr. Yong Pov calls for conservation of archeological sites and halt construction on historical sites
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Yong Pov, Secretary General of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, called for joint conservation of archeological sites and the cessation of construction on those historical sites.
Dr. Yong Pov's appeal was made through a presentation in the presentation of the results of archeological research: new discoveries outside Angkor at the Royal Academy of Cambodia "held this morning, May 9, 2024 At the Tonle Sap Hall of the Khmer Academy, Institute of Humanities and Social Sciences of the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
He said that the values of archeological research have contributed to the important points such as: strengthening and enhancing the spirit of patriotism, historical documents have been compiled for future generations, excavation and revelation of national secrets, Promote the spirit of national unity and strengthen national unity and contribute to boosting the economy through tourism.
Moreover, Dr. Yong Pov also reminded that in the glorious Angkorian era, the great Khmer kings and nobles always paid high attention to the design of the water system, that is, give priority to the benefits. And the value of water because water really contributes greatly to the state leadership, irrigation and agriculture.
In this regard, Dr. Yong Pov emphasized and stressed that because archeological sites are of greater importance to the nation as a whole, in this sense we need to preserve those areas by stopping the construction of other structures on historical sites. That is because the construction over the archeological site really seriously affects the historical evidence of the nation.
In addition, Dr. Yong Pov also confirmed that even the Royal Academy of Cambodia Techo Sen Russey Trip Park has many historical sites, such as the Angkor Iron Slate. Seeing this important reason, the Royal Academy of Cambodia has been paying attention to the conservation of the park area.
Dr. Yong Pov encouraged archaeologists to continue their efforts on archeology for the nation of Cambodia and for historical evidence for humanity.
