Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, mentioned the history of Ang Ta Minh pagoda, stating that the location of Ang Ta Minh pagoda was previously a rice field where the owner of the land was named Ta Minh. Ta Minh gave the land to the monks, and the monks decided to name the pagoda Ang Ta Minh in 1898. Currently, Ang Ta Minh pagoda uses another name, Wat Kork Chambok.
He continued that the naming of Wat Kork Chambok because this pagoda has a large Chambok tree. Ang Minh pagoda is now 126 years old and has the presence of sacred power, which makes Buddhists and people very confident.
