Before taking office as Prime Minister, Samdech President Hun Manet was known to like to ride big motorbikes after work, but now, due to his duty for the nation and the motherland, Samdech stated that he no longer has the opportunity to ride like this and only looks at rubber motorbikes. Just to relax.
Maybe they know that I have run out of opportunities to use the real thing and try to buy these two rubber motorcycles for me just to watch when I am bored.
Thank you for your understanding. "Now, even though I can no longer ride a motorcycle for fun, I can relax by looking at old photos and two plastic motorcycles on the table." Singapore suspends training of F-16 fighter jets after crash on Wednesday
SINGAPORE (Reuters) - Singapore's Defense Ministry has announced that it has decided to suspend all F-16 training activities after one of its heavy aircraft crashed during a training flight on Wednesday. This was released by Reuters on Thursday, May 9, 2024.
The Singapore Ministry of Defense said the suspension was a safety measure that would continue until an investigation showed it was safe to resume training. On Wednesday this week, the crew safely detached the seat from the plane before an F-16 crashed into the ground at Tengah Air Force Base, leaving the pilot in a stable state of consciousness.
In a statement on Wednesday night, Singapore's Defense Ministry said the pilot had more than 2,000 hours of experience flying F-16 fighter jets and a detailed investigation was under way. According to the pilot himself, he encountered problems with the flight control system during take-off from Tengah base for regular training.
