Father sentenced to 30 years in prison for murder of 2-year-old son
(Phnom Penh): The President of the Trial Chamber of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on the afternoon of May 8, 2024, held a hearing to announce the verdict in the case of a father who killed his two-year-old son and hid it. It took three days for the bathroom to be found, prompting a surprise 30-year prison sentence.
The court also ruled that the father of the murderer could appeal if he did not agree with the decision (as required by law).
There was a murder case when a father killed his two-year-old son and hid his body on a bathroom shelf for three days before finding the body, causing a surprise at 4 p.m. October 23, 2023, at a rented room along Street 310, Village 1, Sangkat Toul Svay Prey I, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Phnom Penh.
The body of the victim boy named Rayuth, 2 years old, now lives with his grandmother and aunt near the scene.
The assailant was named Phuong Thi, 36 years old, a scavenger, staying at the scene. His wife, Sim Romduol, 42, is a scavenger and uses drugs.
According to sources at the scene, the child had been missing for three days and his aunt and grandmother had been searching for him but could not find him until the afternoon. The suspect went to look at the bathroom shelf and found the body of the child victim lying on the shelf covered with a cloth and a doll, and ran out to tell the neighbors.
