Ministry of Economy Spokesperson: Ministry of Economy and Finance spokesman Meas Sok Sen San said: The sub-national administration's budgeting (reducing unnecessary expenditures) is a precautionary measure to prevent and mitigate some of the risks that may arise at the end of the year.
Speaking to Fresh News on May 8, 2024, he explained that by looking at the revenue situation and based on the results of 2023 and the results of the implementation at the beginning of 2024, the Royal Government must revise the budget, which is Precautionary measures should be taken to avoid collisions or the impact of budget expenditures at the end of the year.
"This is a precaution of the government," he said. Therefore, we have issued measures for this sub-national level to review some expenditures and send them to the Ministry for review. "So here are some precautionary measures to prevent some problems by the end of the year if something happens."
Mr. Meas Sok Sen San said this after the Ministry of Economy and Finance issued a circular on the revision and strengthening of budget expenditures of sub-national administrations for the implementation of the Law on Finance for 2024 management.
First. Completely suspend the transfer of revenue from the distribution of tax revenue of the Capital and Provincial Administration to the Municipal, District and Commune Administration. In this regard, the municipal, district and commune administrations must suspend all development projects that use or relate to the revenue from the transfer of revenue from the distribution of tax revenue.
Third. Provincial administrations other than the above five provincial and provincial administrations must carefully monitor the implementation of their revenues. If necessary, the provincial administration shall adjust or reduce expenses, especially unnecessary administrative operating expenses or unnecessary local development expenses, according to the actual revenue situation of the provincial administration in order to rebalance the budget.
Fourth. Municipal and district administrations must closely monitor the implementation of their revenues. If necessary, the municipal, district and Khan administrations shall align or reduce expenses, especially unnecessary administrative operating expenses or unnecessary local development expenses, according to the actual revenue situation of each municipal, district and Khan administration in order to maintain the budget balance. Back.
Fifth. Commune / Sangkat administrations must adjust or reduce costs, especially unnecessary administrative operating expenses, and adjust the budget for 2024 management by incorporating and utilizing the 2023 budget surplus as much as possible to implement projects or action plans affected by Suspend the credit received from the distribution of tax revenue of the Capital and Provincial Administration.
