Cambodian Representative Participates in the 4th Round of the Periodic Review (UPR) Report in Geneva, Switzerland
As a member of the United Nations, Cambodia, like other countries, has an obligation to prepare and submit a UPR report to the United Nations every four and a half to five years, and to participate in the review of this report. In the form of constructive dialogue with representatives of other countries in order to share the best practices and challenges in promoting and protecting human rights in each country.
Please note that the Royal Government of Cambodia has already submitted and actively participated in the review of the UPR report for three rounds. The fourth round of the UPR report is a summary of the achievements that Cambodia has made in the field of human rights in response to the 173 recommendations that Cambodia accepted during the review of the third round of the UPR report in 2019.
Please reiterate that the Human Rights Council's Periodic Review Mechanism is not a forum for humiliating, criticizing or attacking each other on human rights issues, but for a constructive dialogue between states. Share or exchange best practices, experiences, shortcomings or challenges to ensure the promotion and protection of universal human rights.
It is noteworthy that despite the difficult situation during the outbreak of Kovid-19 and other global crises, the competent ministries and institutions have worked hard to implement the 173 recommendations, which is a reflection of the strong will. Cambodia's sharp nose in promoting and protecting human rights.
