Samdech Techo Hun Sen Sends Condolences on the Death of Kim Sieb, Advisor to the Royal Government of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate, sent a message of condolences to Mrs. Reach Sinh over the death of Mr. Kim Sieb, an advisor to the Royal Government of Cambodia and a former Deputy Director of Samdech Techo's Cabinet.
In his condolence message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen wrote, "My wife and I are saddened and saddened to learn that His Excellency Kim Sieb, the husband of Lok Chumteav, passed away on Wednesday, the 1st of Pisak in the year of Rong Chhasak. BE 2567 is on May 8, 2024 at 4:45 at the age of 86 years old.
In this sad time, my wife and I would like to express our deepest condolences to Lok Chumteav and her family for the loss of their beloved husband, father, grandfather, great-grandfather, dear and priceless. A role model for wives, children, grandchildren and all close relatives.
The death of His Excellency Kim Sieb is the loss of an important human resource who sacrificed his physical and mental strength to serve the country in all circumstances in order to serve the national interests in the past.
HE Lay Samkol Donates 10 Million Riels on the Occasion of the 161st Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2024
(Phnom Penh): His Excellency Lay Samkol, Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the Senate, donated 10 million Riels to join the Cambodian Red Cross on the occasion of the 161st Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent May 8, 2024.
His Excellency Lay Samkol regularly donates money to the Cambodian Red Cross every year on the occasion of the 161st Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, and also contributes to various campaigns of the Head of Government and To many other charitable events.
Minister of Rural Development inspects the construction site of 6 roads, the condition of roads and bridges in Tram Kak district, Takeo province and Bor Seth district, Kampong Speu province.
(Kampong Speu): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, inspected the construction site of 6 roads, the condition of roads and bridges in Tram Kak District, Takeo Province and Bor Seth District, Kampong Speu Province.
The first line is a double paved road (DBST) with a length of 3,970 meters, a width of 8 meters, 1 meter on each side, and some artistic structures connecting Trapeang Sra Nge village to Ang Tnaot Khang Lech village, Ang Ta Som commune, Tram Kak district, which achieved 73% .
The third line is a three-story paved road (DBST) with a length of 3,385 meters, a width of 8 meters and a side wall of 1 meter.
Line 6 is 5,500 meters long and 6 meters wide, connecting Tnot Chum village to Damnak Khlong village, O'Saray commune at the request of Tram Kak district authority through the Department of Rural Development of Takeo province.
In response, the Minister also instructed the Takeo Provincial Department of Rural Development to study to build this road in 2025.
After inspecting the road construction site, the Minister and the delegation continued to inspect the condition of a 40-meter-long dilapidated wooden bridge that the people had united to build for use during the rainy season in Dambok Khpos village, Phong commune, Bor district. Economy of Kampong Speu province.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia for May 9, 2024.
Low pressure covers the Gulf of Thailand, the Kingdom of Cambodia, the central Mekong Basin and the South China Sea, the ministry said. This situation will make: From 9 to 11 May 2024:
1. Lowland area: * Minimum temperature 24 ° C and maximum temperature 36 ° C. Winds from the southeast and southwest average 2.5 meters per second. Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap, Battambang, Pursat, Kampong Cham, Svay Rieng, Prey Veng, Kandal, Takeo and Phnom Penh are likely to experience rain with thunder, lightning and gust covering 25% of the area.
2. Upland areas: * Minimum temperature 24 ° C and maximum temperature 37 ° C. Winds from the west and southwest have an average speed of 3.5 m / s. Oddar Meanchey, Preah Vihear, Tbong Khmum, Kratie, Stung Treng, Pailin and Cardamom mountain areas may receive rain with thunder and gust covering 10% of the area.
