Despite the reopening of the port, the United Nations High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR) has reported no aid to Gaza as no staff were available after the Israeli invasion. Took control of the nearby Rafah border crossing on Tuesday, which remained closed.
Israel's limited invasion of Rafah does not signal the beginning of a full-scale invasion of the city that Israel has previously threatened. However, the continued closure of the two main ports could worsen the humanitarian situation in Gaza, where the United Nations has warned of severe famine in the north.
Last week, the United States suspended arms shipments to Israel over fears that Israel could launch a full-scale offensive on Rafah, deepening divisions between the two allies.
