(Battambang): The National Center for Combating AIDS, Dermatology and Sexually Transmitted Infections (NCHADS) in collaboration with the National Authority for Combating Drugs (NACD) on May 8, 2024, organized a training course on interview techniques for biological surveys. Sexual Behavior and Estimating the Number of Injectors and Drug Users in Cambodia in 2024.
Brigadier General Yin Yoeut, Deputy Director of the Department of Education and Public Relations of the General Secretariat of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, stated that the purpose is to estimate the number of drug users and the prevalence of HIV and STIs. Gonorrhea, gonorrhea, hepatitis C) among drug users in Cambodia.
This training course lasts for 4 days from 7 to 10 May 2024 in Battambang province in the presence of Dr. Ngov Bora, Deputy Director of the National Center and consists of officials and staff from Phnom Penh, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang Prey Veng, Kampong Cham, Siem Reap, Preah Sihanouk and Kandal, a total of 50 people.
According to the 2023 report, Cambodia has 23,046 drug addicts and controlled users.
The Minister of Interior requested the Capital and Provincial Road Safety Sub-Committee to work hard to implement the Road Traffic Safety Action Plan effectively.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Aphisant Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Road Safety Committee, requested the Capital and Provincial Road Safety Sub-Committee to make more efforts to implement the traffic safety action plan. Road 2024 of the National Committee for Road Traffic Safety (NCSC) to be effective and successful in reducing road traffic accidents.
According to the Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of the Ministry of Interior, due to the fact that according to the road accident report in the first quarter of 2024, the situation is the same as in the first quarter of 2023, there has been no decrease. A total of 781 accidents occurred, killing 387 people and injuring 1,084 people, with an average of nine accidents per day, resulting in four deaths and 12 injuries.
The Deputy Prime Minister also instructed all road users to remember that only a responsible spirit to respect the law on land traffic, increasing caution at all times on the road, morality, understanding, tolerance is the only way to avoid From traffic accidents and always get safety on the road.
On that occasion, the Minister commended the General Secretariat of the NCC and the Battambang Provincial Road Safety Sub-Committee for organizing the 15th National Road Safety Week in connection with global events. Successfully.
Please be informed that the 15th National Road Safety Week is jointly organized by the General Secretariat of the National Road Safety Committee and the Battambang Provincial Road Safety Sub-Committee.
National Road Safety Week is a United Nations-initiated event designated in May each year in countries around the world to commemorate people around the world, especially in the region. Asia-Pacific, including Cambodia, to focus on improving road safety.
