General knowledge: Ak Yum temple, although not huge, used to be the first mountain temple in Khmer history
(Siem Reap): Most of Prasat Phnom is a royal temple built by the king to dedicate to the deity in the religion of the state, but since the beginning of the Khmer Empire, our Khmer ancestors often built the royal temple of the king on the mountain. However, due to the relocation of the capital and the location of the new capital without the mountains, the ancestors also built the royal temple in the form of a temple on a high, multi-storey hill, that is, a mountain temple.
It should be informed that Ak Yum Temple was first discovered by the French in 1932 during the French colonial period.
