BANGKOK: Thailand's newly-appointed finance minister said this week that he was ready to hold talks with the governor of the Central Bank of Thailand to push fiscal and monetary policy in the same direction. . According to Reuters.
The minister, who is also the deputy prime minister, said he believed the central bank governor would say what was true and reasonable and that the two should be able to work together.
Pichai's comments came amid disagreements between the Thai government and the Bank of Thailand over interest rates, which Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said were too high and hurt the economy.
On Friday, the daughter of influential former Thai Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra also said the central bank's independence was an "obstacle" to tackling the economic crisis, the latest in a string of attacks. In the ongoing dispute over interest rates. According to Reuters.
Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Banteay Meanchey Province Celebrates the 161st Anniversary of the World Red Cross Red Crescent Day May 8, 2024
(Banteay Meanchey): The Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Banteay Meanchey Province this morning, May 8, 2024, celebrated the 161st Anniversary of the World Red Cross Red Crescent Day on May 8, 2024 under the theme "Together with the Cambodian Red Cross for Communities "Healthy and weather resistant."
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and Chairman of the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Government Working Group, and attended by Mr. Blake Vary, Chairman of the Provincial Council, Mr. Oum Rath, Governor of Banteay Meanchey, Deputy Governor. Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, Provincial Gendarmerie, Military, Charity, Officials, Philanthropists, Businessmen, More than 1,000 people.
Mr. Oum Rath continued that the establishment of the Cambodian Red Cross with Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen as the President of the Cambodian Red Cross to alleviate difficulties and help all kinds of vulnerable people everywhere to reduce poverty and help Protect the dignity of vulnerable people and promote humanitarian values of humanity through the core areas of work.
Mr. Oum Rath added that over the past several months, the Cambodian Red Cross branch in Banteay Meanchey province has distributed humanitarian donations to thousands of vulnerable families, including helping thousands of people in Sangsy. Winds, fires, landmines, lightning strikes and droughts, poor and helpless families, and social welfare assistance, people living with HIV, traffic accidents, and more.
In that regard, Mr. Dith Tina wished all the ladies and gentlemen, including their families good health, strength, success in all tasks, received the four blessings of the Buddha, and pledged that the Cambodian Red Cross in Banteay Meanchey Province will use these assistance. To target humanitarian as well.
Two strong men angry at the same wife, one stabbed in the neck and the other stabbed in the abdomen
(Phnom Penh): A man on a tricycle used drugs to the point of breaking drugs and had an argument with his wife, then stabbed himself in the neck with a pair of scissors, causing serious injuries and bleeding at the time of the shock. Nearly 5 pm on May 7, 2024 in Prey Tea 2 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The man, 35-year-old Sok Chandarith, a tricycle rider living in the village, suffered a sore throat, while she was his wife when her husband fled on a motorcycle. The man has been arguing with his wife and often harassing his family because of his drug use.
However, when he arrived in Prey Prey Pring North 2 village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Sen Chey, the tricycle broke down. The man left the tricycle on the road and walked home with bloody wounds. At that time, the people in Prey Pring Khang Cheung village were shocked and reported to the police at the 3rd Chao Chao Post for interrogation.
At that time, the police did not know what happened to the man, so they questioned him, and the man did not answer very well, then the police contacted the family and found out that the man was addicted to drugs and had an argument with his wife. And stab yourself.
In another case, a man stabbed himself to death with a sharp knife, but did not die and suffered serious injuries because his wife and siblings blamed him for not working hard. The family was then transported by tricycle to the emergency room at Lam Bunthon Polyclinic near Chumpouvorn Market.
This incident happened at almost 5 pm on May 7, 2024 at the crematorium of Wat Chumpouvorn 1, Chumpouvorn 1 Village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
The man, Puth Seiha, 31, lives in a rented house in Ang village, Sangkat Choam Chao III, Khan Por Senchey, and was born in Daun Keo city, Takeo province. This is the second time that this man has tried to end his life like this.
According to sources, before the incident, the man was blamed by his wife and siblings for not working hard, causing him to be upset and even quarrel with his wife.
According to the source, construction workers and monks at the pagoda were shocked when the family arrived immediately and took the man on a tricycle to the emergency room. A private polyclinic nearby. Spokesman for the General Commission: Another 357 vehicles were inspected and fined on May 08, 2024
