(Svay Rieng): Two girls, siblings, struggled to collect scrap metal to sell to help their parents support their daily life and education, on May 8, 2024, received gifts from the authorities and philanthropists.
The two girls received a donation from the Svay Rieng Municipality with food and 40,000 Riels. Separately, Mr. Pheng Vannak also donated $ 500 to buy clothes and school supplies to alleviate the suffering of the two girls' families.
The two girls, who are struggling to pick up scrap metal to sell to help their parents make a living, have appealed to philanthropists to donate money to buy clothes and school supplies. One of the two siblings excels at school every year.
Chhorn Pina, a 10-year-old girl in the 5th grade at 2 Thnou Primary School, Sangkat Prey Chhlak, Svay Rieng City, described with a sad face that due to the poor family life outside of school hours, she and her sister often went to collect scrap metal to sell to support their parents. Family life and for buying clothes and school supplies.
The two girls have a father named Yang Chanthy, 42 years old, a construction worker and a mother named Uy Sakhom, 36 years old, collecting scrap metal. My eldest daughter, Uy Srey Roth, 13 years old, is in the 6th grade at 2 Thnou Primary School, she is the best student every year, and my younger sister, Chhorn Pina, 10 years old, is at the 2nd Thnou Primary School, Sangkat Prey Chhlak, Svay Rieng City.
Mr. Yang Chanthy, the father, described that before he lived in Chhouk village, Krasaing commune, Romeas Hek district, due to his poor living conditions, he decided to bring his wife and children to live in Svay Rieng city. He works as a construction worker, while his wife collects scrap metal to sell and buy rice for daily consumption.
Please note that at present, my niece lacks school uniforms and study materials, please kindly help to fund the purchase of clothes and school supplies for these two girls. Preah Serey Samphear Dr. Eng Phalla advises monks to respect the rules and regulations of the pagoda and the school as a monk and a scholar.
