Taliban denies Pakistan's allegations over Afghanistan bombing of Chinese engineer
KABUL: The Taliban-controlled Defense Ministry on Wednesday denied illegal allegations by Pakistan that Afghanistan was involved in attacks on Chinese engineers as relations between the two countries escalated. The two are increasingly tense at a time of heightened insecurity. This is according to the release by Reuters on Wednesday, May 8, 2024.
At a news conference on Tuesday, the Pakistani military said a suicide bombing in March in the northern province of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa had killed five Chinese engineers by the Afghan government. Afghanistan.
Relations between Afghanistan and Pakistan have been strained in recent months, with Islamabad saying Kabul was not doing enough to deter militants targeting Pakistan, and since March, Pakistan has been working. The airstrikes targeted Afghan territory.
