(Phnom Penh): The Asian Vision Institute and the Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs have worked together to strengthen political geopolitical research and analysis, which is an important and indispensable task in each country.
To get started on Monday, May 6, 2024, Dr. Chheng Kimlong, President of the Asian Vision Institute and Research, Analysis and Forecasting Team of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, represented by Dr. Ny Sam Ol, Team Leader Signed a Memorandum of Understanding on "Political Geopolitical Research and Analysis".
The event was chaired by Dr. Sok Siphana, Honorary Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Asian Vision Institute, NORITADA Morita, Chairman of the Board of the Asian Vision Institute, Dr. Un Kheang, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, and Dr. Khy Sovann Ratana, Secretary of State of the Ministry. Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation.
During the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding, there was also a roundtable discussion on "ASEAN Geopolitical Update 2024-2025" with the participation of senior experts and about 30 participants.
The collaboration and partnership between the Asian Vision Institute and the Analysis and Forecasting Research Team (AVI-IRAG) covers a wide range of research topics on topics such as geopolitics, economic development, social policy, environment and domestic political analysis. Member of ASEAN, the Mekong Sub-region and the Asia-Pacific.
Both sides expressed a positive outlook and a strong commitment to deepening cooperation and partnerships on key research and analysis to promote long-term cooperation partnership.
