(Kratie): A gas station at Kilo 88 in 2 Thnou commune, Snuol district, Kratie province, was claimed by the authorities and officials to have been built incorrectly by pouring water higher than the road and not as a canal. For water to flow when it rains, that is, rain flows on all roads, affecting public roads and traffic on the road.
According to the police, the gas station has been banned several times by the District Unity Command as well as relevant professional officials since it started hitting the foundation, which is suspected to be technically incorrect.
During November 2023, a team from the Snuol District Administration Office, led by Mr. Houy Chandani, Deputy District Governor, represented the district governor, led a team to inspect the construction site of the gas station at Heng Simalen.
During a recent inspection of the site, authorities as well as officials found that the overflow was higher than the road, causing water to flow almost completely onto the road. At one end, water could not flow into the sewer.
In particular, the construction of this gas station has been revealed that it is not in accordance with the master plan issued by the Ministry and allowed to build yet, the authorities and officials request the owner of the station to make the correct adjustments.
According to the official, Heng Simalen, the owner of the gas station, did not seem to cooperate with the team and complained that he had already applied for a permit from the Ministry of Lands, the Provincial Department of Public Works and Transport, and the Provincial Cadastral Office. .
