Officials: Extreme weather causes turmeric yields in Kampot and Battambang provinces could fall by more than 50%
From May is the time in some provinces such as Kampot, Battambang to start harvesting durian to supply the local market.
Chhim Vachira, director of the Battambang Provincial Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, told Fresh News that this year's durian yield has dropped significantly compared to last year. Currently, farmers growing durian in Battambang province have been affected by the hot weather, which caused the durian fruit to crack on some trees, with the stalks falling and breaking because many ponds and streams dried up, causing a lack of water. Irrigation.
The director of the Department of Agriculture estimates that durian production in Battambang province has decreased by about 50 to 60%. He said that in Battambang province, durian can be harvested in the third week in May to the second week in August. As for the market price of durian this year, he has not been able to estimate yet, while last year it was between 14,000 riel to 18,000 riel per kilogram.
Mr. Teng Van Thoeun, Deputy Director of the Office of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampot Province, told Fresh Nesws on May 8, 2024 that durian is a crop that needs enough irrigation water and regular watering to flower. And good fruit. However, due to the hot weather this year, flowering and fruiting have been affected and yields have dropped significantly.
According to Mr. Van Thoeun, last year the durian crop in Kampot province received about 15 tons per hectare.
Uon Chheang Meng, president of the Duren Teuk Chhou community in Kampot province, said that durian farmers in Kampot province were not only affected by the hot weather, but also by wildfires, which left many hectares dead. He estimates that Kampot Duren will drop by about 50% this year.
He said that although yields were declining, prices were not good due to the quality of durians. Currently, Kampot Duren Manthong type costs more than 20,000 Riel per kilogram, while Ouk Khak type costs more than 10,000 Riel per kilogram.
He said that while yields were falling and prices were not rising, durian farmers in Kampot province suffered heavy losses as they spent more on farmers' inputs such as pesticides and fertilizers and maintenance.
He said the impact of durian crops from this year's hot weather could also affect next year's durian yields due to unhealthy durian trees.
According to data from the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampot province, by the end of 2023, the area under durian cultivation in Kampot province was 2,345 hectares, of which 1,428 hectares were harvested. In 2023, Kampot Duren harvested more than 20,000 tons.
In Battambang province, a total of 625 hectares of durian was cultivated, of which 417 hectares were collected. Each year, the average yield is 12 to 13 tons per hectare.
