Pursat Provincial Administration issues information clarification regarding the publication of 117 families to help check the conservation of the eel road "O 17 point 1500 foothills"
(Pursat): Pursat Provincial Administration on May 7, 2024 yesterday issued a statement regarding the publication of social media, which published the case of 117 families, requesting the leadership to help check the case. Preserve the eel road "O point 17 at the foot of the mountain 1500".
In the statement, it was stated that on May 6, 2024, there was a live broadcast on the social media of KH Plus News Facebook account related to the case of 117 families, requesting the leadership to help check the case. Preserve Andong Ang Road at O17 point, Dey Krahorm village, Anlong Reap commune, Veal Veng district.
Regarding this case, Pursat Provincial Administration has informed the public and all media:
First, the eel road of the 1500 mountains in the Phnom Samkos Wildlife Sanctuary is the unparalleled natural tourism potential of Pursat province as well as the Kingdom of Cambodia, which is a delightful scene for national and international tourists.
Second, due to the rich properties hidden in the forest of the valley, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the former Prime Minister, who is currently the President of the Senate of Cambodia, was nicknamed "Hidden Flower" and this title has attracted the public's attention. Satisfied and stuck in the heart of each person forever.
Third, the care, protection, conservation and restoration of green cover on the road Eang Ang or Bopha Lak Lon is to fulfill the wishes of the people in Pursat province as well as people throughout the country and international tourists. Come and relax, soak up the cool, fresh air and admire the unparalleled scenery.
Fifth, to mention in the live broadcast that the Pursat provincial administration to dismantle the houses and other crops is the opinion of a small number of people who are only incited by outsiders. So far, the Pursat provincial administration has not forced or instructed any residents to dismantle it.
Sixth, although the conservation of the Eel or Hidden Bopha Road has served the public interest greatly for the general Cambodian people, especially the people in Pursat province, the provincial administration continues to pay attention to the interests of the people. Great too.
