The National Assembly was born from the people for the people
(Phnom Penh): The 7th National Assembly was born on July 23, 2023, a historic event in which more than 84% of the population went to the polls to elect MPs from 18 parties. More than 82% of the people voted for the CPP, winning 120 seats in the 125-seat National Assembly. FUNCINPEC won five seats.
On this basis, the leaders of Cambodia, especially the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, made the right decision to transfer the leadership mandate to the next generation of young leaders, Samdech Moha Bovathipati Hun Manet, who is a young man with active intelligence. And energetic, both intellectually and spiritually.
The first session of the National Assembly of the 7th legislature opened on August 22, 2023 under the highest presidency of His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
