The following is a congratulatory message: Pich Chenda community has ambitions to supply safe vegetables in the Cambodian market for people's health
(Battambang): While people are concerned about the health of Ponleu Thmey Agricultural Community, Pich Chenda is ambitious to supply more agricultural vegetables, especially safe vegetables in the Cambodian market. This is according to Mr. Hun Vutha, President of Ponleu Thmey Agricultural Community, Pich Chenda, who told the media during a meeting with Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on May 7, 2024.
Ponleu Thmey Pich Chenda Agricultural Community was established in 2009 and has not focused on vegetables. Farmers have grown potatoes, corn, soybeans, etc. Later, the community started to produce fruits such as: Ta Nen and Mango. But growing those fruits also has some challenges.
He added that we currently have very few vegetables, but our goal is to have more vegetables, especially safe vegetables. Currently we have cabbage, cauliflower, cauliflower (cauliflower, blue cauliflower, yellow cauliflower, purple cauliflower and orange cauliflower), kale, tomatoes, cherries and Hawaiian peppers.
At the same time, Mr. HUN Vutha stated that the cultivation of vegetables by a clear production group to control the production plan has a clear market, but when we grow without a compilation, we can not know the market for a limited number of consumers. Clearly, if we do not plant, it can be a problem.
