(Kampong Thom): Mr. Say Kim Lam, Governor of Stong District, Kampong Thom Province, on the afternoon of May 7, 2024, presided over a ceremony to visit and hand out equity cards to poor people in Bralay commune, Stong district, Kampong Thom province.
Addressing local people on the occasion, he said that the proper provision of equity is a significant contribution to reducing poverty in local people. In addition, it also contributes to the promotion of the family economy and the national economy.
At the same time, he also reminded the registrar and relevant professional officers to expedite the preparation of some necessary personal documents of the people who need to get the equity card as soon as possible so that they can get the equity card in time and get the benefits. Many such as free treatment in the hospital and receive a monthly allowance.
Mr. Say Kimlam also instructed the Pralay commune administration to divide the roles and responsibilities in direct interview with technical officers to the homes of poor families directly for the efficiency and trust of the general public.
It should be noted that the equity card distributed to parents, siblings, people on this occasion, there are 569 cards, of which 237 poor 1 and 330 poor 2.
Thirteen Families Affected by Typhoon in Ta Kream Commune Receive Humanitarian Donation from Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch in Banan District
(Battambang): On the afternoon of May 7, 2024, the working group of the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch in Banan District, led by Mr. Sreng Sokha, Chairman of the District Sub-Branch Committee, and his colleagues invited and brought humanitarian donations from philanthropists through the District Sub-Branch. Thirteen families were affected by the typhoon on the evening of May 6 in Ta Kream commune, Banan district, Battambang province.
Speaking in a friendly atmosphere with the people, Mr. Sreng Sokha brought a message from Mr. Sok Lou, Chairman of the Branch Committee, especially Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to inform the vulnerable people. All of them stated that he and Samdech always pay attention and care for the well-being of all people, regardless of caste, color, religion or political affiliation.
With the gift of alleviating all these difficulties, Samdech Kittipritthbandit always pays attention to the health of the people, so through today's ceremony, he also reminded all the people to take care of their health by drinking boiled water. Live hygienically and take care to protect your health during hot weather.
For women who have small children or are pregnant, please go to the specialist hospital at least 4 times and have to give birth at the health center, and if you are sick, please hurry to the nearest hospital or health center. On time, do not procrastinate, which endangers life.
The district sub-branch chief reminded people to pay attention to safety when traveling on the road to avoid traffic accidents, because in the past, many people were disabled due to the war, but now we live Under the umbrella of peace, we must not allow ourselves to become disabled due to traffic accidents.
All the people expressed their deep gratitude to the Cambodian Red Cross under the leadership of Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, who is a humanitarian mother who always cares about the well-being of the people without any discrimination.
(Phnom Penh): Both the gunman and his accomplices who shot a group of youths on Street 70, Sangkat Srah Chak, Khan Daun Penh were arrested by the Criminal Department in cooperation with the Phnom Penh Municipal Police under the direct command of General Sar Thet, the National Police Commissioner. Arrested and arrested.
Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner, told Fresh News that the gunman who shot and wounded a group of youths was arrested by the Daun Penh District Police Force in cooperation with the Daun Penh District Police Force. Yes.
Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin, who led the crackdown police force, further stated that after researching and receiving clear information on the night of May 7, 2024, he led the criminal police force in cooperation with the local police force of Russey Keo district to besiege. And arrested another faction near Samhan Market, Sangkat Toul Sangke.
According to the commissioner, when the police siege, the perpetrators fired six shots at the police, but fortunately did not injure the police and the people at the crackdown.
A report from Fresh News Agency from the operation site said that when the specialized police force surrounded and arrested the gunman, he refused to surrender and fired at the police, forcing the police to open fire. Go back to arrest immediately.
After the arrest, the suspect was sent by the police to the Phnom Penh Municipal Police for further questioning.
Please be reminded that at around 2:00 AM on May 7, 2024, a shooting incident occurred on Street 70, Stop R3 in Srah Chak Sangkat, Daun Penh District, causing a young man to be seriously injured. He was taken to Calmette Hospital while the gunman escaped.
According to reports, the reason for the gunman to explode was because he was angry with his girlfriend.
