Mr. Yang Pak was arrested and sent to Prey Sar Prison in January 2024 for public defamation and incitement to discriminate on the basis of Preap Kol's complaint. The lawsuit comes after Yang Pak used a Facebook account called Chivann Pen, also known as Ta Prok, to accuse Preap Kol of being involved in the loss of CIC money.
The indictment was described by Preap Kol as a serious breach of his honor, dignity and integrity.
In the letter, Mr. Yang Pak stated that what he had written so far had no clear evidence or basis. The writing was based on rumors from a small number of investors at CIC, and there was outrage at the loss of promotional accusations against Preap Kol.
Mr. Yang Pak highlighted that after learning that Mr. Preap Kol had no role at CIC, he became even more remorseful and remorseful for his mistakes.
Apologizing for his mistakes, Mr. Yang Pak also asked Mr. Preap Kol to facilitate legal proceedings to pave the way for his release.
Upon receiving the apology, Preap Kol wrote on Facebook that Yang Pak was the first person he was forced to sue in order to protect his integrity.
Mr. Preap Kol said that he was not a very pious person, but the fabrication of information, accusations and slander against him in connection with embezzlement or embezzlement affected his core values and reputation. For decades with difficulty.
Although the slander through Yang Pak's writings hurt Preap Kol countless times, Preap Kol accepted the apology.
However, Preap Kol refused to stop the court proceedings. He claims he has no authority to influence the court proceedings. In addition, he believes that Cambodia needs to implement the law to strengthen the rule of law and the justice system.
Russia's foreign ministry has confirmed that the case is not politically motivated and does not involve espionage. The state-run TASS news agency quoted local authorities as saying the issue appeared to be a normal criminal.
