The military exercise will include exercises in preparation and deployment for the use of tactical nuclear weapons. Here are some things to know about tactical nuclear weapons, and through this nuclear exercise, what is the message that Moscow wants to send to the West:
* What is a tactical nuclear weapon? A tactical nuclear weapon refers to a type of nuclear weapon that is used specifically to take advantage of the battlefield, not a nuclear weapon capable of destroying an entire city from the earth. Tactical nuclear weapons can be mounted on short-range ballistic missiles, artillery or bombers.
In contrast to the strategic nuclear weapons under the arms control treaty between Moscow and Washington, tactical nuclear weapons are not subject to any arms treaty restrictions. Russia has never confirmed how many tactical nuclear weapons it has, while Moscow is believed to have 2,000 tactical nuclear weapons, 10 times more than the United States.
Victims of strong winds in Sangkum Thmey district and fire victims in Kulen district receive humanitarian donations from the Cambodian Red Cross
