(Tokyo, Japan): On May 7, 2024, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, accompanied by many Cambodian investors, is visiting Japan.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol and Cambodian investors will pay a three-day visit to Japan from May 7-9. The current visit of the Deputy Prime Minister and Cambodian investors in Japan is another effort to attract Japanese investors to invest in Cambodia.
The above separate meetings were held with the aim of seeking cooperation to promote business between Cambodia and Japan.
In these important meetings, the Deputy Prime Minister thanked his Japanese counterpart for always supporting the Council for the Development of Cambodia in organizing cooperation projects as well as activities to promote and attract investment to contribute to the promotion of Japanese investment flows to Cambodia. .
The Deputy Prime Minister also informed the Japanese side about the current investment environment in Cambodia, which is open, attractive and convenient for investment in all sectors.
In addition, the Deputy Prime Minister highlighted the Royal Government's efforts under the long-term visionary direction of Prime Minister Hun Manet to maintain political stability, macroeconomic stability and other supportive policies. Cambodia to become a high-income country by 2050.
In the above meeting, the Deputy Prime Minister presented and explained the legal conditions, technical studies as well as the environmental impact assessment of the Prek Chun Funan Techo canal project, which is a project to connect the historic waterways of Cambodia. Nation: The docking of two Chinese ships at Ream Port is to train the Cambodian Navy to use ship skills and test the port, not to set up a military base
(Phnom Penh): General Chhum Socheat, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of National Defense, said that the docking of two Chinese ships at Ream Port is to train the Cambodian Navy to use ship techniques for the Cambodian Navy and to test Chinese-built ports. It is a military base like the foreign media with political tendencies.
The statement by a Cambodian Defense Ministry spokesman came after RFA and some foreign media outlets attacked a Chinese ship dock at a Cambodian naval base, accusing it of setting up a Chinese military base in Cambodia. Cambodia is the second largest foreign military base in the world.
The Royal Government of Cambodia, both under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and now under the leadership of Samdech Hun Sen, has repeatedly stated that Cambodia does not allow foreign military bases in its country and does not violate its constitution. The body is absolute.
With this reaffirmation, a spokesman for the Ministry of National Defense hopes that Cambodia's repeated and clear statements will eliminate the distortions and misrepresentations of foreign media and rumors surrounding the foreign military base. More.
Last April, some foreign media outlets also accused the Prek Funan Techo project of providing opportunities for a Chinese military presence in Cambodia. In response to this accusation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also responded to 6 points.
Phnom Penh Police Search and Crack Down on 6 Gunmen Who Killed a Group of Youths in Daun Penh District
(Phnom Penh): The gunman who fired 6 shots at a group of youths, causing injuries in the middle of the night on May 7, 2024 in Daun Penh district, was arrested by the light criminal office of the Commission. Phnom Penh police have investigated and cracked down.
The operation to arrest the gunman took place around Samhan Market in Russey Keo district on the night of May 7, 2024, under the direct command of General Sar Thet, General Commissioner of the National Police, and Lt. Gen. Chuon Narin, Deputy Commissioner and Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commissioner who led the operation at the crackdown.
According to reports from the operation site, when the specialized police force surrounded and arrested the gunman, he refused to surrender and fired at the police, forcing the police to fire several shots to arrest him. The perpetrators arrived.
However, the identity of the gunman and the origin of last night's shooting has not been confirmed by the authorities because the perpetrator is being sent to the Phnom Penh Police for questioning.
Please be reminded that at around 2:00 AM on May 7, 2024, a shooting incident occurred on Street 70, Stop R3 in Srah Chak Sangkat, Daun Penh District, causing a young man to be seriously injured. He was taken to Calmette Hospital while the gunman escaped.
