Please note that the purpose of the forum, the forum between the Royal Government and the sub-national administration aims to consult between the Royal Government and the sub-national administration to jointly assess the progress, challenges, determine solutions and set orientation. Policy section to accelerate the implementation of the decentralization and deconcentration reform program to help build the foundation for achieving the Cambodia Vision 2050.
Banteay Meanchey Military sends 3 suspects to court in drug trafficking case
(Banteay Meanchey): In the morning of May 7, 2024, the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Gendarmerie sent three suspects and some exhibits to the Provincial Court for legal action in the case of drug trafficking, storage and use. .
It should be noted that on May 6, 2024, the local force of the Serei Sophorn Municipal Gendarmerie, led by Brigadier General Sok Leng, the Commander of the Municipal Gendarmerie, cracked down on drug trafficking, storage and use at the bridge. 4 in Kampong Svay village, Sangkat Kampong Svay, Serey Sophorn city, Banteay Meanchey province, detaining 3 suspects, including:
Colonel Sok Leng said that before the crackdown on the above cases, the local police force of the Municipal Gendarmerie received information from residents that there were cases of active drug trafficking and use at the above point.
He immediately led the force to the scene and saw five suspects selling drugs, and the force arrested three suspects. The other two suspects escaped. The force then brought the three suspects and the confiscated exhibits to the Serei Sophorn Municipal Gendarmerie Base for processing.
After being arrested and interrogated, the three suspects confessed that they had actually trafficked, stored and used illegal drugs. Based on the confession and the actual evidence, the local force of the Municipal Gendarmerie has prepared a case file and sent it to the Provincial Gendarmerie Command to proceed with the procedure.
Colonel Chea Dara, Deputy Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie in charge of anti-drug work, said that the crackdown was also authorized by Brigadier General Born Bin, Commander of the Provincial Gendarmerie and coordinated the procedure. From Mr. Keut Vannareth, Prosecutor of the Provincial Court. Minister of Health urges attention to strengthen OWSO and make it effective to provide services to citizens quickly
