Samdech Techo Hun Sen Meets Mr. Min Ong Lang on Video
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of May 7, 2024, Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia, met with Senior General Min Ong Lang, Chairman of the State Administrative Council of the Republic of the Union of Myanmar on video. .
To begin with, Samdech Techo expressed his pleasure to meet Mr. Min Ong Lang again and thanked him for his congratulatory message on the occasion of his election as President of the Senate. He said the talks were aimed at visiting each other and sharing updates on developments in Myanmar.
In response, Mr. Min Ong Lang once again congratulated Samdech Techo on his election as President of the Senate and thanked Samdech Techo and highly appreciated Samdech Techo's participation in his visit to Myanmar. Contribute to resolving the Myanmar issue while Samdech is chairing ASEAN.
Taking that opportunity, Samdech Techo also once again asked Mr. Min Ong Lang to consider arranging a video meeting between Samdech Techo and Ms. Aung San Suu Kyi for the purpose of visiting because Samdech Techo and she used to be many colleagues. Years in ASEAN Affairs.
At the same time, Samdech Techo stressed the importance of implementing the five-point unanimous agreement and hoped that this progress would contribute to the peace process, with Myanmar itself as a leader and owner.
Samdech Techo also welcomed the decision of the State Administration Council to send non-political representatives to the Foreign Ministers' Meeting in January and encouraged Myanmar to continue appointing representatives to key ASEAN meetings.
In response, Min Aung Lan agreed to continue sending his non-political representatives to the ASEAN Summit and promised to consider other proposals with the utmost care and to send his special envoy to Cambodia in the near future to continue to discuss these proposals and to accept the sharing of good experiences from the National Election Committee of Cambodia related to the organization of a free, fair and transparent election.
The two leaders also discussed and exchanged views on cultural and sports cooperation.
