In April this year, the Council for the Development of Cambodia approved 22 investment projects with a total investment of more than $ 309 million.
(Phnom Penh): In April 2024, the Council for the Development of Cambodia approved 21 new projects and 1 project to expand production with a total investment of 309 million US dollars and can create about 23,000 jobs. This is according to the press release of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News on May 7, 2024.
The Council for the Development of Cambodia stated that of the 22 investment projects located outside the SEZ, 14 were investment projects and 8 were located within the SEZ.
It should also be noted that the most prominent investment projects in April include:
A: Outside SEZ 1: Investment project to produce socks, gloves, scarves, hats, and indoor shoes, located on National Road 1, Samaki Village, Sangkat Svay Toeur, Svay Rieng City, Svay Rieng Province, with an investment capital of approximately 9 Million US dollars and can create about 2,000 jobs.
It should be noted that in April 2024, investment from China ranked first, contributing up to 98% of total investment. Minister Net Pheaktra led the leadership and officials of all levels of the Ministry of Information to test drugs
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of May 7, 2024, the Ministry of Information, in cooperation with the National Authority for Combating Drugs, conducted a drug test within the framework of the Ministry of Information, which has a total of 1,840 civil servants, advisors and contracted officials. People at the Ministry of Information.
On that occasion, Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, said that the drug test is a campaign to achieve the commitment "Cambodia is a drug-free country and keep each family a clean family drug-free from the perspective Join together for a drug-free life and community. ”
He continued that the work of drug testing in the ranks of civil servants at all levels of the Ministry of Information was carried out in accordance with the implementation of the order of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Royal Government of Cambodia No. 01 dated. February 20, 2024 on the introduction of strict measures in the fight against illegal drugs in ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations.
At the same time, the Minister stressed that "we all have an obligation to test for drugs, including me." Therefore, as an example to other civil servants, the Minister of Information and Chairman of the Commission for the Promotion of Education of the Anti-Illegal Drug Campaign also conducted drug testing and was followed by leaders and civil servants from the General Department of Specialization.
The Minister wished all the leaders and civil servants good results and would like to thank Dr. Neth Savoeun, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, for providing technical assistance. Drug Testing and thanked all the leaders and assistants for their active participation in fulfilling this important duty.
According to the report of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, as of April 29, 2024, a number of ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations have been assigned to implement this regulation by conducting rapid tests for drugs in the water. Urine on civil servants, national police officers, soldiers and contracted officers, a total of 56,445, including positive results, drugs in the urine of 76 people who were expelled from the framework.
