"One Nation Standing System" is another new achievement of the Royal Government in its efforts to improve the business environment, promote trade and promote economic growth in Cambodia.
The "One-Stop-Shop" system will allow exporters-importers to apply for licenses, permits, certificates, and other required documents related to the export-import of goods to all competent ministries and institutions in one go. Each to obtain permission for use in completing the customs clearance form electronically.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Mani President Hun Manet's opportunity to officially announce the implementation of the "One Nation Standing System":
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet expressed his pleasure to participate in the announcement of the implementation of the one-nation stand system.
* President Hun Manet stated that the introduction of a one-stop-shop system reflects the Royal Government's proactive and highly responsible efforts to improve business in Cambodia.
* Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet highly appreciated and commended the Chairman, Vice Chairman and all members of the Steering Committee of the One Nation Standing Project for their joint efforts to develop and implement this One Nation Standing Project until it was successful.
* President Hun Manet stated that Cambodia is among the countries with the highest economic growth in the region and in the world. Prior to the Kovid-19 crisis, Cambodia achieved high economic growth at an average rate of 7% per year, which allowed Cambodia to transform from a low-income country to a low-middle-income country in 2015.
* Prime Minister Hun Manet stated that the Royal Government has always made improving the business and investment environment and trade facilitation a top priority, setting out policies, strategies, programs, and reform measures, as well as legal standards. For continuous improvement - practical implementation.
* President Hun Manet stated that this achievement is a continuation of the deepening reform and modernization of the tax administration to increase the efficiency of revenue management and create fair competition in business and investment and to reduce costs. On the fulfillment of fiscal obligations and procedures.
* President Hun Manet stated that the one-nation stand-alone system will be a key player in the digital ecosystem for business, making our trade facilitation more efficient and able to connect to the digital ecosystem for other businesses. Local and global.
Samdech Hun Sen strongly hopes that the one-nation stand-alone system will be another successful example of the joint efforts of the ministries and institutions of the Royal Government to overcome the difficulties in the institutional coordination process.
Samdech Samdech Hun Manet instructed relevant ministries and institutions that have not yet participated in the implementation of the one-stop-shop system to promote the participation of this system as soon as possible for the ministries and institutions that have already participated and must continue to pay attention to implementation. Work with high quality and efficiency.
* Samdech Manipadei Hun Manet instructed the Steering Committee of the One National Standards Project to monitor and evaluate the implementation and continue to improve and expand the system functions, as well as expand the connection to other information technology systems related to business and trade to continue. Meet the actual needs of the business.
* Samdech Manipur Hun Manet urges the private sector to participate and make the most of this one-nation control system and to provide feedback for improvement.
* Samdech Thipdey Hun Manet instructed the Ministries and Institutions to continue to pay close attention to the work of promoting the business environment and facilitating trade, especially to promote the successful implementation of the measures set out in the Royal Government-Private Sector Forum. The 19th time on November 13, 2023.
