Ministry of Water Resources announces weather conditions in Cambodia for May 7, 2024
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has issued a notification on the weather situation in Cambodia for May 7, 2024.
Low pressure covers the Gulf of Thailand, the Kingdom of Cambodia, the central Mekong Basin and the South China Sea, the ministry said. This situation will make: From 7 to 9 May 2024:
1. Lowland area: * Minimum temperature 25 ° C and maximum temperature 36 ° C. Winds from the southeast and southwest have an average speed of 3.5 m / s. Banteay Meanchey, Siem Reap, Battambang, Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Cham, Svay Rieng, Prey Veng and Kandal provinces may experience rain with thunder and gust covering 15% of the area.
2. Upland areas: * Minimum temperature 24 ° C and maximum temperature 36 ° C. Winds from the west and southwest have an average speed of 3 m / s. Oddar Meanchey, Preah Vihear, Mondulkiri, Tbong Khmum, Kratie and Cardamom mountain areas may receive rain with thunder and gust covering 20% of the area.
3. Coastal areas: * Minimum temperature 24 ° C and maximum temperature 35 ° C. Southwesterly winds average 2.5 meters per second. Koh Kong, Sihanoukville, Kampot and Bokor mountain range may experience rain with thunder and gust covering 20% of the area. Wave height has a minimum average height of 0.50 meters and a maximum average height of 1.50 meters. Mr. Hun Many met with the structure of the People's Movement of the Cambodian People's Party in Siem Reap
(Siem Reap): Mr. Hun Many, Member of the Standing Committee and Secretary General of the Mass Movement Committee of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party, met with the structure of the Siem Reap Mass Movement Committee.
Attending the above ceremony were the leaders of the General Secretariat of the Mass Committee, the Central Committee, the members of the Provincial People's Movement Committee, the Municipalities, the Districts and the Communes and Sangkats throughout Siem Reap, a total of 570 people.
Mr. Prak Sophoan, Chairman of the Provincial Party Committee and Chairman of the Siem Reap Provincial Party Movement Committee, thanked and warmly welcomed the presence of Mr. HUN Many and reported the progress of the Public Movement Committee to the Secretary General and Delegates who paid tribute to the Party Committee and the Provincial Mass Movement.
After listening to the report of the Provincial Party President, the Secretary-General praised all the working groups who have worked hard to build the past achievements.
Mr. HUN Many confirmed that all members believe in the leadership of the Royal Government led by the Cambodian People's Party and with Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Vice President of the Cambodian People's Party as the Prime Minister.
"The trust that comes from the people needs to be built on a regular basis and takes a long time to get," he recalled.
It should be noted that the above meeting was organized in order to strengthen the structure and role of the party's mass movement at the local level of the party to contribute to ensuring the victory of the party in all upcoming elections.
