Cambodia, Indonesia Sign Memorandum of Understanding on Aircraft Accident and Accident Investigation
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Mao Hovannal, Minister in Charge of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, this morning, May 6, 2024, signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Air Force Accident and Accident Investigation with Dr. Ser Chan Tochjono, Chairman of the Committee. National Transport Safety Authority of Indonesia will open a training course on air accident investigation.
Mr. Sin Chanserivutha, Undersecretary of State and Spokesman for Civil Aviation, stated that during the ceremony, Dr. Mao Havanal recalled the history of relations between Cambodia and Indonesia, establishing diplomatic relations in 1957. Since the establishment of diplomatic relations, Indonesia has been a strong supporter of peace and stability in Cambodia.
The Minister expressed his pleasure to attend the signing of the Memorandum of Understanding on the Investigation of Air Accidents and Incidents between the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation of Cambodia and the National Committee for Transport Safety of the Republic of Indonesia. This collaboration demonstrates a shared commitment to improving aviation safety and ensuring a thorough and effective investigation into aircraft accidents and incidents.
"The exchange of skills and knowledge between the two nations will definitely strengthen our ability to conduct a comprehensive and transparent investigation that ultimately contributes to the safety and security of the two countries' skies," he said.
"Today is also the start of training on air accident investigations conducted by experienced Indonesian investigators," said Minister Mao Zedong. "This training opportunity is invaluable because it will equip our aviation experts with the necessary techniques and skills to handle complex, clear and diligent investigative operations."
He stressed that a successful training program that will not only benefit their respective countries but also contribute to the advancement of world aviation safety standards. 161st Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2024
