Ministry of Agriculture, Ministry of Rural Development and Ministry of Water Resources issue joint press release on the outcome of the first tripartite meeting on "Agriculture, Rural Development and Water Resources"
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Chhay Rithy Sen, Minister of Rural Development and Mr. Thor Chetha, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, jointly chaired the meeting on Monday, May 6, 2024. Discuss on agriculture, rural development and water resources.
The tripartite meeting was held for the first time at the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries with the participation of leaders and professional officials of the three ministries.
Through lively discussions, the three ministers, co-chairing the meeting, agreed in principle on four key points, including:
1: Set strategic goals, which are the common priorities of the three ministries by putting forces and resources together to implement successfully.
2: Consult with each other according to their respective skills and fields regularly and consistently to prevent and overcome obstacles in order to achieve the set goals.
3. Linking projects and policy programs related to the communities of the three ministries, such as the modern agricultural community of the Ministry of Agriculture, the community of farmers using water of the Ministry of Water Resources and the model village project of the Ministry of Rural Development to help local people. Get the maximum benefits.
4: Agree in principle to establish an inter-ministerial working group to work together consistently and set up a regular meeting every three months to monitor the work set out and determine the work plan. Duke Chhin Song and Lok Chumteav (Tow Chhin Seng Co., Ltd.) Donate $ 2,000 on the 161st Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2024
