She added that the sale of Amret's shares to SinoPac Bank will bring new growth to the microfinance institution and that Amret will continue to serve its customers as usual. She could not comment further.
The acquisition of one of Cambodia's leading microfinance institutions will take place in three phases, with the first phase to acquire 80 per cent for about $ 435 million, while the second and third phases will acquire the same 10 per cent. Together at the end of the first year and the second year.
According to a press release issued by SinoPac Holdings on May 4, 2024, the acquisition of Amret is in line with its strategy, with one of the company's four main strategies being to "increase "Revenue abroad and expand our international presence."
However, the Taiwan-based company said that the acquisition of Amret, which has already been approved by its board of directors, will go through a number of stages and conditions, including approval. According to other relevant regulations as well.
MFIs are Cambodia's largest deposit-taking microfinance institution in terms of total assets. As of December 31, 2023, Amret has 150 operating branches in 24 provinces and cities across Cambodia with total assets of US $ 2 billion.
Bank SinoPac, which has been lending to Amret since 2017, will be able to expand its overseas service network in Southeast Asia through this acquisition, the statement said. The company's resources and expertise, combined with the existing products of Amret Microfinance Institution, will help Amret provide a wide range of financial services and convenience.
