Ministry of Education announces the recruitment of 15 youth delegates to participate in the 48th Southeast Asian and Japan Youth Ship Program
The 2024 General Assembly event welcomed more than 200 delegates from ASEAN countries and Japan to attend the Board of Directors' Meetings, Country Reports, Forum, Discussions, Study Visits and Visits of Performing Arts.
* Cambodia will host 2025 At the closing ceremony of the 33rd International Congress of the Southeast Asian and Japanese Youth Ship Program, Mr. Hor Samnang received the flag to host the 34th General Assembly, which will take place on May 1-4, 2025 in Siem Reap Province. Next year's event is expected to attract more and more participants from ASEAN and Japan.
Mr. Hor Samnang said in his speech at the hosting ceremony, "I invite all participants to come to the Kingdom of Cambodia to visit the ancient capital and rich cultural heritage of Cambodia, get to know the friendly Cambodian people. Friendly and understand the current situation and progress of Cambodia under the cold shadow of peace, stability and progress in all areas.
The event will showcase and enhance Cambodia's prestige to visitors from ASEAN and Japan, and contribute positively to the economy and tourism of Siem Reap.
It should be reminded that Cambodia has already hosted this General Assembly event twice in 2007 and 2016 with great success, with close cooperation with the General Department of Youth of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. Sports and support from other ministries and institutions of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
