Gaza: Palestinian security sources and eyewitnesses report that Israeli warplanes have launched air strikes on areas east of Rafah. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on May 6, 2024.
The raid caused a massive explosion and caused severe damage to a nearby building, but no casualties have been reported so far.
Prior to the attack, the Israeli army ordered the evacuation of Palestinian civilians from the eastern city of Rafah. Israel considers Rafah the last major stronghold of Hamas. Rafah is located in the southernmost part of the Gaza Strip bordering Egypt and is home to about 1.4 million Palestinians.
Israel launched a major offensive against Hamas in the Gaza Strip on October 7, 2023, following the group's shocking attack on southern Israel, which killed about 1,200 people.
