(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Information, in collaboration with the Ministry of Posts, has been preparing cards for journalists linked to QR Codes to prevent fraud as journalists and to act in violation of professional ethics. This was confirmed by Mr. Tep Asarith, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Information in the Fresh Talk program last weekend.
He stressed that this will make the media in Cambodia order in advance and all journalists will be valuable. However, he said that once a new press card is available, journalists must also perform an ethical profession, otherwise only the card will be cut.
The spokesman for the Ministry of Information also stated that as a journalist, it is very important to study the journalism profession before going out to work as a journalist, because in the past, there were journalists, especially those who hold Live phone as a journalist violates the privacy of others, and all of these actions also affect the professional journalists.
Listen to the spokesperson's remarks:
According to Mar Yarith, this case is no different from the implementation of the professional ethics of journalists, because if the rights and freedoms of journalists affect the rights of others, they also face the same law. Mr. Mayarith made such a statement during a discussion on Fresh Talk last Saturday.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mar Yarith, President of the FTC Information Training Center, expressed his opinion that the report on "Freedom of the Press in Cambodia" by the Ministry of Information was based on a more accurate approach than some civil society organizations have done in the past. More. Not only that, it is obtained from the planet, which is an unidentified journalist, which puts pressure on commentators.
As the President of Fresh News Vocational Training Center, Mr. Mar Yarith expressed his support and pride for a report that Cambodia can do on its own, be independent, not under pressure and pressure from others, that this report can make Cambodia Present to the international arena about Cambodia's press freedom directly.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tep Asarith, Undersecretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Information, claimed that the field of press and freedom of the press in Cambodia today is much better than ever compared to the past of the country. Cambodia. The spokesperson's claim was made in a live talk show on Saturday last week.
Not only that, Mr. Tep Asarith also confirmed that the state of press freedom was assessed by journalists who participated in random surveys, not targeting or arresting only those who have a tendency to support the government. The survey found that 79.8 percent of journalists claimed to have full freedom of the press.
To know more, please watch the discussion of Mr. Tep Asarith as follows: Senior Minister Ieng Moly co-chairs the 2nd Joint Meeting of the Royal Government - Development Partners in Response to HIV / AIDS in Cambodia
The meeting also aims to jointly consider the achievement of the agreed goals and ensure the sustainability of the HIV / AIDS response in accordance with the National Policy on HIV / AIDS and the Sustainability of the AIDS Program for 2023-2028, contributing to the Pentagon strategy. The first of the Royal Government, led by Samdech Thibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The meeting discussed the role and responsibilities of the Joint Working Group of the Royal Government - Development Partners on HIV and AIDS in Cambodia, National Policy to End HIV / AIDS and the Sustainability of the AIDS Program for 2023-2028: Updates, Next Steps and Joint Activities and Civil Society Forum: Issues related to coordination, mobilization, resources and partnerships.
At the same time, we are short of funds for preventive work while the Global Fund grant remains. What can the rest of the money do to help prevent it? Therefore, we will propose a budget adjustment. Before concluding, the Senior Minister stated that we listen to what is being said and will study with stakeholders to improve the shortcomings and find ways to correct them.
In conclusion, the Senior Minister thanked the Director General of UNAIDS, the Co-Chair of the Ministries, Institutions, National and International Organizations, Representatives of People Living with HIV / AIDS, for attending the meeting, and especially thanked the United States, France and Japan, major donors for their support. Responds to HIV and AIDS.
